{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles","id":478606,"title":"Lancea et Sanctum Merits and Miracles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-12T19:19:37-07:00","id":478606,"title":"Lancea et Sanctum Merits and Miracles","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles-playtest-vampire-the-requiem/\" target=\"_blank\">The preview is up</a>. What are your thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T19:24:01-07:00","id":478624,"title":"","content":"Quite a lot of cool stuff in here, but what stood out most to me was Pledge to the Worthless One. Could this mean that Belial's Brood is being recast as a faction of the Lancea et Sanctum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T19:28:29-07:00","id":478625,"title":"","content":"I'm still working through this, but I have to say that the first dot of Crusade bugs me a lot. As far as I know, Crusade is supposed to be more of a mundane fighting style that's good for hunting witches, not a set of faith-based supernatural effects. I could see an effect like having +2 to Resistance rolls against malign magics while having a weapon since it works as a mental focus, but as written someone with Shield Against Sorcery makes it harder to fireball because reasons. It just doesn't make any sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T19:38:32-07:00","id":478631,"title":"","content":"Lots of cool stuff, but a few things that made me strongly scratch my head (as I described in my comments in the actual blog).<br /> <br /> Pledge To The Worthless one is very fitting as an ultimately damning and unreversible sacrifice. And it says nasty nasty things about Theban Sorcery, which I love. (Interesting question in the context of it though, Charlaquin.) Apocalypse and the Judgement Fast are suitably terrifying. But again, the ratings for some of these rituals are all over the place. With all its benefits Apple Of Eden has to be at least a 2 if not a 3 dot ritual, and Miracle Of The Dead Sun should outright be a 5 dot ritual, given it <i>blots out the sun</i> and effectively allows Kindred to act as though it was fully nighttime for the duration. To mention a few.<br /> <br /> Already spoke about my gripe with Crusade in the blog (the second and third dots are fine, but that first is just weird and completely turns me off, which is a shame because I really wanted to like it), but there are very cool merits in this otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 04-12-2015, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T19:44:16-07:00","id":478633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478625#post478625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still working through this, but I have to say that the first dot of Crusade bugs me a lot. As far as I know, Crusade is supposed to be more of a mundane fighting style that's good for hunting witches, not a set of faith-based supernatural effects. I could see an effect like having +2 to Resistance rolls against malign magics while having a weapon since it works as a mental focus, but as written someone with Shield Against Sorcery makes it harder to fireball because reasons. It just doesn't make any sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are parrying that fireball. Heck, they parry your mind control too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T19:44:54-07:00","id":478634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478633#post478633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are parrying that fireball. Heck, they parry your mind control too.</div> </div> </div> </div>God, that sounds so dumb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T19:48:44-07:00","id":478636,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that does seem pretty weird tbh...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T19:53:14-07:00","id":478639,"title":"","content":"Ditto on what Kirby and Faith are talking about.<br /> <br /> I for one am ready for our Sanctimonious Belial worshiping heathen overlords.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T19:53:29-07:00","id":478640,"title":"","content":"Crusade does appear awfully powerful or unusual, particularly without any explanation of just why it works.<br /> <br /> I would expect that its effects should at least require a prerequisite of a few dots in Theban Sorcery. In fact, I believe the effects would would be far better implemented as a mid-level TS Miracle that blessed a particular weapon (maybe the Sacrament could be an actual melee weapon used by a crusader or warrior of faith). In any event, the Kindred Dueling or other fighting style Merits seem to be able to adequately represent the intent of Crusade.<br /> <br /> I also have a question about Apple of Eden. Does &quot;being able to see supernatural creatures for what they are&quot; provide any protection against werewolf Lunacy or the benefits of a Sleepwalker in Mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":".  typo 04-12-2015, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T19:53:43-07:00","id":478641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478633#post478633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are parrying that fireball. Heck, they parry your mind control too.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my entire issue with it. That first dot is basically &quot;SMACK AWAY THE SPELL WITH YOUR WEAPON, ANY SPELL EVEN DIRECT SUBTLE ONES&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which is ridiculous. What is this, Dudes Of Legend? Old World Of Darkness? Katanas And Trenchcoats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T19:56:04-07:00","id":478642,"title":"","content":"The more I think on it the more Belial's Brood as a Sanctum faction fits.<br /> <br /> You're damned anyway. You're going to hell <i>anyway</i>. Why <i>not </i>take the pledge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T19:57:54-07:00","id":478643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478642#post478642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more I think on it the more Belial's Brood as a Sanctum faction fits.<br /> <br /> You're damned anyway. You're going to hell <i>anyway</i>. Why <i>not </i>take the pledge?</div> </div> </div> </div>It does make an absurd amount of sense trying to see it from that light.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T20:02:31-07:00","id":478648,"title":"","content":"So, Aaron's Rod mentions &quot;each success on the Toxicity roll.&quot; That's... Not how poisons work as far as I'm aware...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T20:05:36-07:00","id":478651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478641#post478641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is my entire issue with it. That first dot is basically &quot;SMACK AWAY THE SPELL WITH YOUR WEAPON, ANY SPELL EVEN DIRECT SUBTLE ONES&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which is ridiculous. What is this, Dudes Of Legend? Old World Of Darkness? Katanas And Trenchcoats?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry you find it so ridiculous. I'll try not to make the second draft so worthy of derision. I'll endeavour to make it less viable a target for ridicule than other things that we work on, love, and proudly publish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T20:07:13-07:00","id":478653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478642#post478642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more I think on it the more Belial's Brood as a Sanctum faction fits.<br /> <br /> You're damned anyway. You're going to hell <i>anyway</i>. Why <i>not </i>take the pledge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely! It also explains why they didn't get any mention at all in the Covenants section of B&amp;S - they're not a separate Covenant, they're a heretical splinter group of the Santified.<br /> <br /> And seriously, their ideology makes <i>perfect sense</i> as a radical interpretation of Loginian doctrine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T20:17:07-07:00","id":478682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478651#post478651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry you find it so ridiculous. I'll try not to make the second draft so worthy of derision. I'll endeavour to make it less viable a target for ridicule than other things that we work on, love, and proudly publish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shrug it off. People are not going to like things, no big. Combat Merits are going to get additional scrutiny and hyperbole, but it's not worth responding to if you don't feel it's constructive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T20:17:07-07:00","id":478683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478651#post478651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry you find it so ridiculous. I'll try not to make the second draft so worthy of derision. I'll endeavour to make it less viable a target for ridicule than other things that we work on, love, and proudly publish.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize for coming off as so abrasive. I'm not trying to deride the work the writers put into it or the writers themselves. I'm (harshly) criticizing something I see as poorly explained and/or badly implemented because <i>I want to like it</i> and I want to see the concept behind it, that I do immensely like, shine. The second and third dot of Crusade are in my opinion, well done, and the basic idea is very much in line with how I visualize inquisitors and witch-hunters of the Lancea Et Sanctum.<br /> <br /> I truly didn't mean to offend. I greatly appreciate the work Onyx Path and its personnel do. The post was supposed to be jokingly exaggerated in tone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 04-12-2015, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T20:19:40-07:00","id":478684,"title":"","content":"I actually quite like Crusade, but I do think the first maneuver should apply only to obvious effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T20:24:19-07:00","id":478687,"title":"","content":"Silence seems like it should have a tilt attached to it.<br /> <br /> Also there are no disciplines that use extended actions, but I guess that might change in the future.<br /> <br /> Just looking at a Hammer Against Witches brings up a lot of questions. It doesn't seem to fit the existing sorcery structure. So far the way sorcery works is the 'damage' spells are usually long range, you can target individuals up to a mile away, which was necessary, because due to the extended time it takes to cast, each roll of the dicepool for a ritual is going to be 15 to 30 minutes, 60 if you're using an altar with some untrained, so it's not something you would really do in the middle of combat for a Crusader to take advantage of. Especially since while casting a ritual you lose your defense.<br /> <br /> Then from the Crusader's point of view, they have to sneak up on the ritualist, because any interruption to a rite causes it to automatically fail. And if they do, they can spend willpower to make an attack with a penalty that should do some extra bashing damage and turn that failure into a dramatic one.<br /> <br /> So the questions. Is the damage regular bashing weapon damage as normal with a weapon? If you have multiple people helping in one ritual, does this ability work against the supporting ritualists, or only the leader?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-13-2015, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T20:32:38-07:00","id":478697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478634#post478634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> God, that sounds so dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of things sound really dumb. Like the Invictus' ability to snark people to death (Courtoisie, however you spell it), or how a vampire can make you do what it wants by gazing soulfully into your eyes and saying pretty please (Dominate).<br /> <br /> Doesn't make them less useful, or less terrifying if you're on the receiving end.<br /> <br /> Blood-drinking apex predators don't need your approval, yo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T20:42:45-07:00","id":478705,"title":"","content":"I don't have any problem with crusade's first level, this is a lance martial art after all, so why assume it's supposed to be mundane?<br /> <br /> It's hammer against witches I'm not so sure about, applying both a dramatic failure and doing damage equal to the level of the magical effect, that seems doubly punitive.<br /> <br /> Stigmata- What's the cost for human stigmatics? And why would a mortal character want to be stigmatic, since it provides no actual benefit to them? Wouldn't it make more sense for it to be a merit for the vampire- Stigmatic vessel, since they are pretty much the only one getting a benefit here?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 04-12-2015, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T20:44:44-07:00","id":478707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478697#post478697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of things sound really dumb. Like the Invictus' ability to snark people to death (Courtoisie, however you spell it), or how a vampire can make you do what it wants by gazing soulfully into your eyes and saying pretty please (Dominate).<br /> <br /> Doesn't make them less useful, or less terrifying if you're on the receiving end.<br /> <br /> Blood-drinking apex predators don't need your approval, yo.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, what I'm saying is...look, I don't get &quot;mah versimilitude&quot; very often so bear with me.<br /> <br /> Dominate, other Disciplines, blood sorcery, whatever, usually has some thread of logic backing it up, even if the thread's as tenuous as &quot;vampires are so unnaturally charismatic they can enthrall you via eye contact. Cool, magic. And like I said, if this style was more about faith based supernatural effects, I'd be more fine with it, although outside of making it an explicit Miracle I think it'd be making a statement about the vampiric condition and faith I wasn't particularly happy about, but whatever, there'd be a plausible backing.<br /> <br /> Shield Against Sorcery is the first technique in a mundane style taught to witchhunting crusaders, which somehow leverages mundane knowledge of weaponry into a blanket penalty against magic effects. I just don't -get- that. That doesn't compute. If I -try- to accept that you can make somebody worse at casting mind control spells by just holding a sword or having a pair of knucks on you - not doing anything mind you, just having it out - then the first thing I think of is that everybody else who has ever fought magic-wielding foes are chumps who clearly don't understand how to sword properly. The Adamantine Arrow.are lagging behind the catholic vampires in terms of techniques and strategies to kill magic wielding foes. So the premise falls flat for me for several reasons.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I digress, and unless something new comes up I'm done talking about Shield Against Sorcery since I said my piece and even gave some feedback on why it doesn't work for me and what could be done to fix it. There's other stuff in the preview I'm not thrilled about, but I'll live.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T20:45:30-07:00","id":478709,"title":"","content":"On Crusade: I actually think it makes a lot of sense, as part of the apparent Merit-push to show the Sanctified really do believe in all of that Medieval Catholicism with vampires; forget that idiotic Inquisition business, the Sanctum knows what actual witches look like and can do, and they will protect their human and vampire flock from them. They are devils with <i>faith, </i>dammit, and they're going to use that faith to protect themselves!<br /> <br /> I kind of expect a Crusader has to be aware of an incoming spell to parry it, for the same reason you can't parry a surprise attack. I also agree that you probably have to know your way around Theban Sorcery-I think the thematics would be fixed if you just called it out as an impromptu field rite that turns the symbolism of blocking an spell into...actually blocking a spell. Maybe you need to spend a point of Willpower/Vitae to do so for the scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 04-12-2015, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T20:45:31-07:00","id":478710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478705#post478705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stigmata- What's the cost for human stigmatics? And why would a mortal character want to be stigmatic, since it provides no actual benefit to them? Wouldn't it make more sense for it to be a merit for the vampire- Stigmatic vessel, since they are pretty much the only one getting a benefit here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think being a valued -yes, even holy!- vessel to a group of fanatic monsters is <b>not </b>beneficial?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T20:49:21-07:00","id":478716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478697#post478697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of things sound really dumb. Like the Invictus' ability to snark people to death (Courtoisie, however you spell it), or how a vampire can make you do what it wants by gazing soulfully into your eyes and saying pretty please (Dominate).<br /> <br /> Doesn't make them less useful, or less terrifying if you're on the receiving end.<br /> <br /> Blood-drinking apex predators don't need your approval, yo.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If Crusade is directly magical in nature like Dominate, at least include a few dots in Theban Sorcery as a prerequisite and/or require a willpower point or similar expenditure for Shield.. However, if it's just a fighting style, some explanation should be provided how it can deflect fireballs, no less mind control or magics from other supernaturals like Mages and Changelings. Shield of Sorcery and Hammer Against Witches are also very powerful for one and three dot merits, respectfully. As for Courtoisie, I agree that it similarly suffers from verisimilitude problems, and one incongruous merit does not justify another.<br /> <br /> I also agree with a prior poster that the second dot of Crusade, Silence, should result in a Tilt if it is to be consistent the new 2e combat system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":".  clarification 04-13-2015, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T20:54:34-07:00","id":478722,"title":"","content":"A one dot Theban Sorcery prerequisite would make sense to me. Crusade could be both an application of faith and very particular esoteric technique honed from the Miracles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T20:54:47-07:00","id":478723,"title":"","content":"Crusade seems a bit potent to me for a 1 to 3 dot merit, especially if it works on non-Kindred effects as one of the levels specifically says it does. I think for one, it should require Theban Sorcery so you actually have some divine type power backing what you're doing. Past that, I think it just needs to be a higher dot rating, though I dunno how that meshes with how Styles normally work.<br /> <br /> That being said, while I think it does need balancing work, I actually do like the idea of the divinely backed witch hunting style.<br /> <br /> Sanctuary's really cool, but seems like it'd be better needing 3+ dots of status instead of 2, at least for one of them, as 3 dots has always seemed to me like when you have that kind of authority in a Covenant or the city.<br /> <br /> I really like the idea of Stigmata as a split Kindred/Supernatural merit. Wanted to give props for that.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for rituals, Apple of Eden seems potent for 1 dot (though pretty awesome, otherwise).<br /> <br /> Overall, I like the rituals, like the Cruac ones from the previous update they make much better use of the (subpar, IMO) magic system in 2nd edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T21:04:04-07:00","id":478725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478722#post478722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A one dot Theban Sorcery prerequisite would make sense to me. Crusade could be both an application of faith and very particular esoteric technique honed from the Miracles.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Although I agree about the prerequisite, and have stated such, I believe one of the priorities of Crusade was to actually provide a significant LeS merit that did NOT require proficiency in Theban Sorcery, hence a conundrum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T21:16:00-07:00","id":478752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478682#post478682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shrug it off.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478682#post478682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People are not going to like things, no big. Combat Merits are going to get additional scrutiny and hyperbole, but it's not worth responding to if you don't feel it's constructive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't care if people don't like things. But I ask for a certain amount of basic dignity and respect when our unpolished work is put forth for constructive notes. I spend a lot of unpaid time engaging with the audience in order to get feedback and improve upon the material. I don't think it's an unreasonable thing to ask for some degree of respect and generous reading so we can keep that unpaid time productive, and something we actually want to continue doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T21:21:12-07:00","id":478757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478752#post478752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't care if people don't like things. But I ask for a certain amount of basic dignity and respect when our unpolished work is put forth for constructive notes. I spend a lot of unpaid time engaging with the audience in order to get feedback and improve upon the material. I don't think it's an unreasonable thing to ask for some degree of respect and generous reading so we can keep that unpaid time productive, and something we actually want to continue doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, I think you do great work and love the effort you tend to put into engaging with the forums here (and in your work in general). Helps to make it feel like our input matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T21:22:05-07:00","id":478759,"title":"","content":"I appreciate the call for respect when it comes to these devblogs. I think it's easy to fall into a certain comfortable frankness when we're reacting to this stuff that doesn't always take into account the feelings of the people writing them. I think we can definitely strike a better balance between feedback which is honest and respectful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478725#post478725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I agree about the prerequisite, and have stated such, I believe one of the priorities of Crusade was to actually provide a significant LeS merit that did NOT require proficiency in Theban Sorcery, hence a conundrum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it does have the Occult prerequisite. Maybe discussing it as being some kind of particular Theban Sorcery technique in its description could solve the &quot;issue&quot; as it were without imposing a 3 Experience tax on the merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 04-13-2015, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T21:25:22-07:00","id":478762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478759#post478759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well it does have the Occult prerequisite. Maybe discussing it as being some kind of particular Theban Sorcery technique in its description could solve the &quot;issue&quot; as it were without imposing a 3 Experience tax on the merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my first rough for it, I actually designed it for characters without Theban at all; they required a Merit that literally made them resistant to sorcerous effects, and prohibited them from ever learning a form of blood sorcery. Sort of a mystical eunuch type thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T21:26:48-07:00","id":478765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478762#post478762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my first rough for it, I actually designed it for characters without Theban at all; they required a Merit that literally made them resistant to sorcerous effects, and prohibited them from ever learning a form of blood sorcery. Sort of a mystical eunuch type thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>What made you roll that back? Seems like a good way both to cover that mystic backing (even if more anti-magic than magic) as well as adding a cost to it, given its potency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T21:27:43-07:00","id":478768,"title":"","content":"Apocalypse sounds like it's the Lance's equivalent of Mutually assured destruction, they don't actually use it because it would screw themselves over too, but it's powerful deterrent to action by their enemies.<br /> <br /> Then again, I could see the lance deploying this in a part of town controlled by their enemies to provoke a torches and pitchforks situation against them, but that seems like it could backfire horribly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T21:36:54-07:00","id":478774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478765#post478765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What made you roll that back? Seems like a good way both to cover that mystic backing (even if more anti-magic than magic) as well as adding a cost to it, given its potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see a reason for removing it in not wanting to cut out Sanctified characters who want to use the Covenant's Advantage, which seems fair to me. I've felt in the past that some Merits had unnecessary restrictions, and the ability to have more choices to mix together always feels like a good thing.<br /> <br /> My feedback on the Theban Sorcery rituals themselves: I definitely feel some stuff should get shifted to higher dots. I also think these powers really accomplish the whole biblical feel for the most part. They feel like great set pieces for Chronicles, or as ways to kick them off. So they're an A+ for style, in my book. I could totally see myself using them in plots.<br /> <br /> I think my critique is that some of them almost feel <i>too big </i>like Apocalypse or the one that blots out the Sun. Like they're dope as climactic Chronicle events, but as a player, they feel like rituals I wouldn't be able to/be willing to realistically use more than once in an entire Chronicle. I don't know if that's a <i>bad thing </i>but I will say that one of my favorite things about the great Crone rituals in the Circle's <i>Secrets of the Covenants </i>playtest was that these rituals felt like ones I could regularly use to achieve a signature style for a Cruac witch character.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T21:38:12-07:00","id":478777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478774#post478774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could see a reason for removing it in not wanting to cut out Sanctified characters who want to use the Covenant's Advantage, which seems fair to me. I've felt in the past that some Merits had unnecessary restrictions, and the ability to have more choices to mix together always feels like a good thing.<br /> <br /> My feedback on the Theban Sorcery rituals themselves: I definitely feel some stuff should get shifted to higher dots. I also think these powers really accomplish the whole biblical feel for the most part. They feel like great set pieces for Chronicles, or as ways to kick them off. So they're an A+ for style, in my book. I could totally see myself using them in plots.<br /> <br /> I think my critique is that some of them almost feel <i>too big </i>like Apocalypse or the one that blots out the Sun. Like they're dope as climactic Chronicle events, but as a player, they feel like rituals I wouldn't be able to/be willing to realistically use more than once in an entire Chronicle. I don't know if that's a <i>bad thing </i>but I will say that one of my favorite things about the great Crone rituals in the Circle's <i>Secrets of the Covenants </i>playtest was that these rituals felt like ones I could regularly use to achieve a signature style for a Cruac witch character.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that's true. Of course, they could always reintroduce the merit, and make it an option of either that merit or Theban sorcery. Though, that might make things a bit cluttered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 04-13-2015, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T21:46:57-07:00","id":478798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478774#post478774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could see a reason for removing it in not wanting to cut out Sanctified characters who want to use the Covenant's Advantage, which seems fair to me. I've felt in the past that some Merits had unnecessary restrictions, and the ability to have more choices to mix together always feels like a good thing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, basically that. I didn't want what could be the bulk of characters in a chronicle to be barred from it. <br /> <br /> I liked the idea. I even did a playtest character with the Theban Eunuch concept. But I figured it would be too rare without additional mechanical support.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T21:54:18-07:00","id":478803,"title":"","content":"I mentioned it in the blog comments, but I think Marian Apparition using period blood is a bit weird. Setting aside the creepy (and-not-in-a-good-way) implications as to where exactly you're going to get it, menstrual imagery seems like much more of a Crone thing. For the L+S I could see it being something more like the Blood of a Virgin what with the Mary imagery and all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T21:56:20-07:00","id":478805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478762#post478762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my first rough for it, I actually designed it for characters without Theban at all; they required a Merit that literally made them resistant to sorcerous effects, and prohibited them from ever learning a form of blood sorcery. Sort of a mystical eunuch type thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making a character a form of null or zero magic zone would certainly explain the significant supernatural effects for the first and third dots of Crusade, although I agree with your instincts that the benefits of the merit would not appear to justify eliminating access to the LeS signature ability. However, without the supernatural background / prerequisites for the merit, it unfortunately, at least to me, breaks verisimilitude and is not thematically much different than the Kindred Dueling fighting style in the core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T22:01:15-07:00","id":478808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478803#post478803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mentioned it in the blog comments, but I think Marian Apparition using period blood is a bit weird. Setting aside the creepy (and-not-in-a-good-way) implications as to where exactly you're going to get it, menstrual imagery seems like much more of a Crone thing. For the L+S I could see it being something more like the Blood of a Virgin what with the Mary imagery and all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Crone imagery is not coincidental. Note the side-effect benefit to the use of <i>Cruac </i>rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T00:41:04-07:00","id":478860,"title":"","content":"Quite a few of the spells here are really Cruac-like... with all the blood and stuff. <br /> <br /> As for Crusade (Which seems the most controversial of merits in the batch) - Shield against Sorcery really needs a change. Either a thematic one (my magic voodoo/faith/beans/enchantedweapon does the protection) or a mechanical one (only spells with physical components can be dodged (like fireballs)). <br /> <br /> Also, Laity... I probably write this in every playtest, but seriously. Can't we have a &quot;Fan of X&quot; merit, which gives all these benefits. Since it seems to me they are differentiated by the one last merit provided, it could even said &quot;if you're fan of L+S it's Library, if you're a fan&quot; bla bla... As is now, we got single merit, take up the space of five and as I argued before hand it's not even that good. Mostly anyone would be better off with just buying a Status dot in the said covenant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T00:45:06-07:00","id":478861,"title":"","content":"Aaron's Rod...is the intended use to be gaining a small fairly sneaky creature to go and fetch something for you? Or to just be an impressive bit of sorcery to aid in intimidation or presence style rolls? The poison suggests it;s intended for a combat role but 4 dice to attack?<br /> <br /> Could I instead milk the venom from the snake and use that venom as part of one of my own attacks (with a much higher dice pool)?<br /> <br /> For Crusade. What counts as 'dark sorceries'? Embeds and Exploits? Disciplines? Werewolf Gifts? Spirit/Ghost/Angel Numina/Manifestations/etc., Theban Sorcery?<br /> <br /> Rank 1 specifically says 'that target her' so spells/sorceries/etc. that target an area containing her are valid? So the aforementioned fireball thrown AT her would suffer the -5 penalty ('cos anyone planning on being a sorcerous knight it going to <i>want</i> a maxed weaponry eventually) but an exploding fireball thrown a few feet to her left would suffer no penalty?<br /> <br /> I would not want the Crusader to lose out on Theban Miracles, I like the idea of requiring another pre-req merit to purchase it and I would suggest that pre-req merit grants some level of protection against magical mental influence - and leave Crusade as defending against magical physical attacks. So you can avoid parrying mind control like some manner of Solar Exalt. There's the merit in the GMC Core that gives bonuses to resist mental effects...Indomitable or something that could work?<br /> <br /> For the Rank 2 it allows an attack to the vocal chords without penalty...what's being pictured here? because if I jam a sword through your throat that's one thing but an axe/pollaxe/chainsaw blow is fairly likely to just decapitate you.<br /> <br /> For Rank 3 the intent seems to be interrupting something going on, the extended action discipline or a ritual, does that mean that an instant cast spell (or a spell that was prepared earlier and has a trigger like some of the Theban miracles) could not be interrupted?<br /> <br /> Flock: It says the members of the Flock start any scene with a single point of Willpower, what if a member of the Flock is a fairly important NPC (or a Goul or your Retainer etc.) and could realistically have more than a single point under normal circumstances?<br /> <br /> Hmmm, could Laity would allow you to learn Crusade?<br /> <br /> I could see some fairly questionable - though legal - play with the Sanctuary Merit. Take it and have a few different 4-dot Blood Sorcerors, they may well be stuck in your Safe Place but they can cast their spells out to a very long range. You could also use them to learn the various secrets of the other Covenants. Take a Dracul and Crone criminal in and leverage them to learn the secrets of the other Covenants. Further, is there any penalty to kicking the criminals out of your Sanctuary?<br /> <br /> Does Revelatory Shroud overcome or contest Obfuscate? Clash of Wills it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T07:13:04-07:00","id":479025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478752#post478752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't care if people don't like things. But I ask for a certain amount of basic dignity and respect when our unpolished work is put forth for constructive notes. I spend a lot of unpaid time engaging with the audience in order to get feedback and improve upon the material. I don't think it's an unreasonable thing to ask for some degree of respect and generous reading so we can keep that unpaid time productive, and something we actually want to continue doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree wholeheartedly. The quality of recent material you guys (especially you and Rose) have come up with has been of a certain quality WW had not seen in a long time.<br /> <br /> It's also something I get around my tables, players subjecting my plots to the scrutiny of their logic. In a fantasy world filled with monsters. Oh the vanity of our time, where we think we even get the logic behind how things operate in our, so-called material world.<br /> <br /> I like everything about this write-up, it represents a vision that has been steadily surfacing and love where this is going for what it brings to the stories I write. Keep up the good work, kicking asses and taking names.<br /> <br /> Will do heavy play-testing, once my finals are over (and I graduate!) and post results here. The whole write-up arrived just in time for my Dark Ages Requiem chronicle (c.1100s).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T07:57:02-07:00","id":479041,"title":"","content":"Personally I like the image of a vampire paladin chopping spells in half, but that's just how I roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T08:17:17-07:00","id":479059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=479041#post479041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I like the image of a vampire paladin chopping spells in half, but that's just how I roll.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i know right? I think I'm going to let this fighting style be my 2e Septemi bloodline gift with a few other goodies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T08:24:37-07:00","id":479065,"title":"","content":"Sorry for being crude in my earlier posts, everyone. I was way harsher than it called for, and I edited my post to try to rectify that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478861#post478861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aaron's Rod...is the intended use to be gaining a small fairly sneaky creature to go and fetch something for you? Or to just be an impressive bit of sorcery to aid in intimidation or presence style rolls? The poison suggests it;s intended for a combat role but 4 dice to attack?<br /> <br /> Could I instead milk the venom from the snake and use that venom as part of one of my own attacks (with a much higher dice pool)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Creative. Seems a little gamey, though. Maybe you could just make a slightly lower level spell that just creates a poison straight up?<br /> <br /> Also, I imagine it could serve as an impressive display or a tool of assassination. More than a few people have died in history and in fiction from a poisonous animal in their sheets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478861#post478861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Crusade. What counts as 'dark sorceries'? Embeds and Exploits? Disciplines? Werewolf Gifts? Spirit/Ghost/Angel Numina/Manifestations/etc., Theban Sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they purposefully went for it being general for the sake of versatility. I'd let it be up to a GM at a particular table what they want it to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478861#post478861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would not want the Crusader to lose out on Theban Miracles, I like the idea of requiring another pre-req merit to purchase it and I would suggest that pre-req merit grants some level of protection against magical mental influence - and leave Crusade as defending against magical physical attacks. So you can avoid parrying mind control like some manner of Solar Exalt. There's the merit in the GMC Core that gives bonuses to resist mental effects...Indomitable or something that could work?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a neat idea that Indomitable is perfect for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478861#post478861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Rank 2 it allows an attack to the vocal chords without penalty...what's being pictured here? because if I jam a sword through your throat that's one thing but an axe/pollaxe/chainsaw blow is fairly likely to just decapitate you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see a pommel strike or a shallow cut doing it if it doesn't do a ton of damage. If you're doing it with your 5L Claymore and you get 2 successes, I might just call it a decapitation though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478861#post478861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flock: It says the members of the Flock start any scene with a single point of Willpower, what if a member of the Flock is a fairly important NPC (or a Ghoul or your Retainer etc.) and could realistically have more than a single point under normal circumstances?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd let it give them one extra Willpower, then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478861#post478861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, could Laity would allow you to learn Crusade?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't imagine it would by RAW, but I probably would. These days, I'm imagining the actual membership of the L + S to be much smaller than I thought it was before, since I'm imagining they may draw laity from the other covenants.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T09:44:59-07:00","id":479182,"title":"","content":"So here is a question: Is there a particular reason why there are no Theban Sorcery Styles, like the Cr\u00faac Styles?<br /> <br /> Now, I realise Theban Sorcery by its nature is much more uniform than Cr\u00faac, but I think one could still make interesting distinctions, from quiet, dignified prayer to bombastic spectacle that would make a Pentecostal snake handler proud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T10:04:55-07:00","id":479212,"title":"","content":"I think the thing is Cr\u00faac comes from different sources and has personalized ways of practicing it. But the Theban rituals are rituals that have been static since they were found.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T10:21:39-07:00","id":479222,"title":"","content":"If all that is wanted is a pat on the back, why is there open development going on at all? Weak critisism is often worse than useless, an echo chamber is no place to do development or review. And arguments of tone is also unproductive, in general.<br /> <br /> The Crusade merits seems to enable a very different powerset than anything else in merits, giving the ability to interact directly with powers Vampries are usually unable to manipulate, like Supernal magic or spirit Numina. Versimiltude of setting and mechanics is the most important thing in an RPG ruleset(for me at least), so I would either make the effect less supernatural (+ to resistance) or the description overtly supernatural (require sword and shield annointed in blessed Vitae during a day and night of vigil, for instance, perhaps through a Theban ritural).<br /> <br /> Anyho, with the exception of Crusdade, these are pretty cool. Espeically the Belial's Brood ritual, the apple ritual (which should perhaps be level 2) and the Flock merit. Still, we never play Lancea et Sanctum, they are always antagonists, so I guess I like the ones that are good as NPC inspiration and mechanics the most, and many of these are great for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1228-jhiriit","name":"Jhiriit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T10:31:30-07:00","id":479230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=479182#post479182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here is a question: Is there a particular reason why there are no Theban Sorcery Styles, like the Cr\u00faac Styles?<br /> <br /> Now, I realise Theban Sorcery by its nature is much more uniform than Cr\u00faac, but I think one could still make interesting distinctions, from quiet, dignified prayer to bombastic spectacle that would make a Pentecostal snake handler proud.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like this change, personally. Not mirroring everything between the covenants seem nice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> tho I'm not sure what Theban styles would do... But I also guess there's quite a few biblical images we could conjure there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T10:44:28-07:00","id":479249,"title":"","content":"I think gospel music probably jars with the whole &quot;creature of the night&quot; aesthetic a bit too much though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T11:11:19-07:00","id":479297,"title":"","content":"There is criticism, harsh criticism, and then there is belittling. When it gets to the point that people are making a joke of it, they go too far. Regardless of intent, offense was given, so it makes sense for someone to get upset over it. We should not be criticizing either party because that is well beyond the purpose of this thread.<br /> <br /> I think Crusade is not completely mundane, not intended to be. I would switch the order and make Silence the first dot myself. The issue I have with Shield against Sorcery is using it against spells that could be cast from miles away. It isn't as much a problem with kindred sorcery since the target is aware of being targeted. I'm not sure that is the case with other forms of sorcery. It becomes more of a stretch when using this maneuver to defend another. I think Crusade could use another pass, but I don't have the experience to offer more help with it. It is not nearly as messed up as some have suggested. Let's leave the hyperbole at the door please. This isn't the Exalted forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T11:34:21-07:00","id":479310,"title":"","content":"Criticism is fine. If you don't like the Merits or miracles, go ahead and say so. I'm not going to pay much attention to hyperbole or snark, though. And do try to point out the things you like, because it's useful to know what resonates as well as what you'd like to see adjusted.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the helpful commentary so far. Crusade is, in fact, not purely mundane -- that's where the Occult requirement comes in. But it's also not -- at least in this draft -- actual Theban Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 04-13-2015, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T11:57:52-07:00","id":479325,"title":"","content":"In the case that Crusade isn't mundane, then my critique just boils down to one critique and one gut feeling, which is that a) an up to -5 penalty is -huge- in the system math, especially in a one-dot merit, and b) it seems a little passive that as long as you're holding a weapon you put out that penalty. If it's a Theban enchantment then that's okay, since the magic will have a duration; otherwise, I don't know, maybe it takes a WP to activate for a scene or it works only in battle (ie when running through initiative order). Appreciate the continued consideration on this merit.<br /> <br /> For what little it's probably worth at this point, I - really- like the feel of Silence. It does a specific, tangible effect that -may- stop magic (and happens enough that they developed the technique) but leaves it open to whether it actually works, and the ability to silence folks is useful on its own. I really dig it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 04-13-2015, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T12:19:35-07:00","id":479338,"title":"","content":"I think Crusade is an brilliant concept, though I think it the first dot requires a bit of tweaking. I also feel that making it, and Theban, mutually exclusive wouldn't be a bad idea. I like the idea of the Lance (and the Circle) having sects within with different capabilities. When I write up the Lance and Circle up in my games not everyone is a blood sorceror as not everyone needs it to fulfil their needs/duties. The idea of a Crusader fighting magicks by making themselves an anti-thesis would be a genuinely interesting concept to run with, and would have some neat setting consequences.<br /> <br /> A suggestion to add (though I realise it may be too late to do this in the dev process) - I would like a Lancea et Sanctum specific set of simple rules and a couple of examples of relics. Religious relics seem to already have a niche within the Lance especially, I as a player and DM would <i>love</i> to see some Relic love within the Lance chapter. This is said owning Reliquaries, I would be interested to see the vampiric church's take on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T13:01:22-07:00","id":479372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=479041#post479041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I like the image of a vampire paladin chopping spells in half, but that's just how I roll.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe that many would agree with you, including myself, and would welcome some mechanism for doing as you suggest (within reanson). The criticism of Crusade is primarily that just breaks verisimilitude and is overpowered within the context of 2e mechanics and comparable merits.<br /> <br /> I think that one of the problems is that much of Crusade might be trying too hard to fit into the niche of a significant combat ability for LeS characters that chose not to invest any merit dots in Theban Sorcery.<br /> <br /> After reading the constructive criticism of many here, I would suggest tweaking Crusade as follows:<br /> <br /> 1. Increasing the Occult prerequisite (and/or allow TS as an alternative prerequisite).<br /> <br /> 2. Focusing the merit on a particular designated weapon more than the vampire. In order to gain the advantages of the merit, require some moderately difficult ritual such as to anointing a weapon with Vitae, the blood of a large predator and blessed holy water under a full moon. The magic in the weapon will store for one month per blood potency of the vampire. When facing a magical opponent, the vampire who conducted the ritual can then invoke the magical protection in the weapon (up to Crusade dots) for up to an entire scene.<br /> <br /> If you want to keep with a strict LeS and Longinus theme, possibly only permit Crusade to use a spear as the magic weapon and require a Weaponry specialty with Spears as a prerequisite.<br /> <br /> 3. Make Silence the one dot power and/or alter it to reflect training in removing more targeting penalties besides the throat to disrupt a target's use of magic.. In addition to targeting the throat to affect someone's voice, it could be valuable to target to eyes to induce blindness, wrists and elbows to impede gestures and targeting, etc. The attack also need not be a typical strike, and could include feats such as rustles dusts, leaves or other objects at a target. These special attacks should result in Tilts without damage consistent with 2e combat.<br /> <br /> 4. Add a two dot power similar to the Indomitable or Iron Will merits to resist magical mental coercion or illusion.<br /> <br /> 5. Shield can only deflect direct physical and noticeable attacks like fireballs. No deflecting mind control. A willpower point expenditure might be considered and it should be a minimum 3+ dot power.<br /> <br /> 6. Eliminate or reduce the additional damage of sorcery or discipline level for Hammer or possible cap it at the weapons natural damage modifier.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 04-13-2015, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T14:10:20-07:00","id":479456,"title":"","content":"It would also be possible to let the Crusade have two different prerequisites: one could either know Theban Sorcery, or be a magical eunuch. This way the style would be viable for everyone, but would technically be two styles that work in different ways in fluff, but have the same mechanics. As a Theban user you would need to find a Theban crusader to teach you, and if you are a magical eunuch you need a eunuch crusader. This could be explained by having the magical eunuch style predate the Theban one, where the Theban one was founded to replicate the other's effects.<br /> <br /> And I have to say, I love all the other Merits and Rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T15:38:02-07:00","id":479566,"title":"","content":"Perhaps also make the dice pool modifier for the rank 1 Crusade equal to the dots in the merit rather than equal to Weaponry? Capping the penalty at 3 (i.e.: opponent must spend Willpower) rather than at 5 (leaving some of those other splats that use only 2 stats for their power dice pools in a lot of trouble) and encouraging purchase of the other dots of the style because from my point of view rank 1 is the bit that I want and the other two dots are really not very attractive. Nice to haves but fundamentally if I am hitting a sorceror with a weapon I am probably doing fairly meaningful damage anyway and there are plenty of ways of buffing that damage (blood for more strength, willpower for more dice, all out attack all give more dice for more potential successes), or Vigour. Or called shots as often Rituals or Extended Castings leave their user without a defence.<br /> <br /> A starting character with a single merit dot and 4 dots in Weaponry (the kind of player who <i>wanted</i> to have weaponry 5 at the start but couldn't justify more than a 4 right now) is going to be <i>close</i> to immune to any incidental (i.e.: ones they have but aren't a focus of the character so their attributes and skills aren't gamed a little to help the dice pools on them) Disciplines people have and maybe also some of the more focused ones too.<br /> <br /> Assuming resisted with blood potency+attribute and average values for attributes is 2 this character reduces the dicepools of all (?) Disciplines by 7 dice at character creation.<br /> <br /> If they also take Indomitable they are causing a -9 dice penalty to any of the mental Disciplines like Dominate and Majesty and Nightmare.<br /> <br /> If it's a power that can be defended against then it could be even more of an issue. Athletics 4, Weaponry 4, Dex 2, Wits 2 and a Shield (giving +2 or 3 to the defence, including against ranged attacks) is causing this magical attack to suffer a -12 dice penalty. And that attribute block (Dex 2 Wits 2) is...maybe not the most common on someone focused on being a 'knight' with a sword and shield.<br /> <br /> Note also that against an enemy whose primary form of attack is magical or magical ranged there is no reason not to be in all out attack against them because you're not resisting with your defence anyway.<br /> <br /> I'd be really damned happy spending 3 of my 10 merit dots at creation and 4 of my 11/7/4 skill dots for that. And most of that I'd likely have taken anyway if I were making a Lancea 'knight' so it's really not a hardship or meaningful additional cost.<br /> <br /> Now that may well be the intended result (it makes a Lancea 'knight' really, really, really hard to hurt with magic) but this same character is also really very good at physical violence and has not spent <i>that</i> many resources achieving this state so could happily spend a few merit dots for some allies and connections and having a solid set of social attributes so there is no reason this character needs to be weak socially so the argument of solving all your problems with violence need not come up for this character.<br /> <br /> Basically, if I were playing a member of the Lancea et Sanctum I can't see a reason why I <i>wouldn't</i> take this merit at one dot (and ignore the rest of the powers because those require other supporting expenditures to be worthwhile). Even a single dot of Weaponry on the character makes the merit worth it. So long as taking the merit is not directly deleterious to my concept of course. But Lancea Priest who dabbled in their 'youth' before finding their true calling? Gangrel with Frenzy problems who finds solace in the teachings and disciplined life of the Lancea? Anyone the Lancea are just trying to tempt into the Covenant with some small enticement?<br /> <br /> This would be a merit I would be looking to steal through hook or by crook with merits like the Carthian one that lets you access other Covenant's unique stuff.<br /> <br /> Also, what if your favoured weapon is a stick? Like a jo-staff or other short stick like a...walking stick? You could avoid the most obvious issue of requiring you to be holding a weapon if your weapon is something you could potentially be carrying with you frequently.<br /> <br /> I have nothing against this in concept - I just feel it's far too powerful as it sits right now and it's the kind of thing that would frustrate me as the GM a lot. Because 'and you chop down the enemy wizard/sorceror/ventrue/etc. with little threat to yourself' gets a bit repetitive after a while.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T18:14:26-07:00","id":479689,"title":"","content":"I tend to be a fan of giving a bonus or penalty that scales with dots in a Merit, so I'll give that some thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T20:28:27-07:00","id":479823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478710#post478710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think being a valued -yes, even holy!- vessel to a group of fanatic monsters is <b>not </b>beneficial?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Considering that the lancea practices would disgust the vast majority of human stigmatics, and that the benefit is essentially being the pig who is too tasty to eat all at once, the answer I'd come with is &quot;Hell to the !##$$# no.&quot; <br /> <br /> Being a human stigmatic is Grade A premium nightmare fuel territory- being locked in a closet, blood bound, or dominated into being a human ant so that some vampires who make ISIS look like nice moderates rain death, torment, and corruption on one's loved ones. Pass, thank you. <br /> <br /> Now if Stigmatics had, or could buy lancea status, to show that the lancea see them as holy vessels worthy of respect and cooperation, that would be a merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T21:02:18-07:00","id":479856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=479823#post479823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Considering that the lancea practices would disgust the vast majority of human stigmatics, and that the benefit is essentially being the pig who is too tasty to eat all at once, the answer I'd come with is &quot;Hell to the !##$$# no.&quot; <br /> <br /> Being a human stigmatic is Grade A premium nightmare fuel territory- being locked in a closet, blood bound, or dominated into being a human ant so that some vampires who make ISIS look like nice moderates rain death, torment, and corruption on one's loved ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that like it's a bad thing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T21:10:12-07:00","id":479870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=478683#post478683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I apologize for coming off as so abrasive. I'm not trying to deride the work the writers put into it or the writers themselves. I'm (harshly) criticizing something I see as poorly explained and/or badly implemented because <i>I want to like it</i> and I want to see the concept behind it, that I do immensely like, shine. The second and third dot of Crusade are in my opinion, well done, and the basic idea is very much in line with how I visualize inquisitors and witch-hunters of the Lancea Et Sanctum.<br /> <br /> I truly didn't mean to offend. I greatly appreciate the work Onyx Path and its personnel do. The post was supposed to be jokingly exaggerated in tone.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's cool. No worries. <br /> <br /> (Just wanted to make that clear. I liked your post initially, so I hoped you'd get the notification. But I didn't want to be ambiguous here.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T21:14:09-07:00","id":479875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=479182#post479182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here is a question: Is there a particular reason why there are no Theban Sorcery Styles, like the Cr\u00faac Styles?<br /> <br /> Now, I realise Theban Sorcery by its nature is much more uniform than Cr\u00faac, but I think one could still make interesting distinctions, from quiet, dignified prayer to bombastic spectacle that would make a Pentecostal snake handler proud.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly I ran out of space. I worked with Filamena when she was writing the Circle of the Crone section, and she asked me if I could do X, Y, and Z. That sounded a lot like what the Styles ended up looking like. That didn't really occur when I was writing the Lance stuff. I also rather like most of the Lance stuff, particularly some of the Theban. It rolled along rather well. So, I went with the momentum when writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T21:16:48-07:00","id":479878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jhiriit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=479222#post479222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If all that is wanted is a pat on the back, why is there open development going on at all? Weak critisism is often worse than useless, an echo chamber is no place to do development or review. And arguments of tone is also unproductive, in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say anything about the first few comments on Crusade. I appreciated the feedback. However, simply chiming in to second a criticism, by levying an insult at our OWoD products in order to make fun of our NWoD products is not constructive at all. It literally added nothing to the feedback outside of insults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T23:02:21-07:00","id":479945,"title":"","content":"I liked seeing some fleshing out of the notion that this covenant has a sort of exorcist or demon hunter faction within it. The concept has been around before R2, but now it is getting some meat. I therefore enjoyed the concept behind Crusade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T23:38:39-07:00","id":479953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=479945#post479945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked seeing some fleshing out of the notion that this covenant has a sort of exorcist or demon hunter faction within it. The concept has been around before R2, but now it is getting some meat. I therefore enjoyed the concept behind Crusade.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wasn't there a bloodline in V1 that was essentially anti-magic knight? the Septimi? Septimus? Their Discipline was Abjurism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T00:58:14-07:00","id":479997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=479953#post479953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasn't there a bloodline in V1 that was essentially anti-magic knight? the Septimi? Septimus? Their Discipline was Abjurism?</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent and on-point recall!<br /> <br /> The Septemi from <i>Ancient Bloodlines</i>, pp. 90-97 (Your comment encouraged me to look them up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). The powers and effects of the Abjurism Discipline certainly appear to achieve much of what Crusade intended thematically and mechanically, and is an excellent framework in which to take a second look at the Merit (if it wasn't already considered by the authors).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T01:50:08-07:00","id":480010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=479997#post479997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Excellent and on-point recall!<br /> <br /> The Septemi from <i>Ancient Bloodlines</i>, pp. 90-97 (Your comment encouraged me to look them up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). The powers and effects of the Abjurism Discipline certainly appear to achieve much of what Crusade intended thematically and mechanically, and is an excellent framework in which to take a second look at the Merit (if it wasn't already considered by the authors).</div> </div> </div> </div>It was definitely considered. I love the Septemi. They're one of my favorite bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T02:44:43-07:00","id":480031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=479856#post479856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You say that like it's a bad thing...</div> </div> </div> </div> Well maybe we have different views on what merits ought to be.<br /> <br /> To me, a merit should be something advantageous to the character, even if it has major drawbacks.<br /> <br /> To a human stigmatic, there's no benefit, just an existence that makes the future of an expert in ancient and obscure languages in a call of cthulhu game seem as cheery as that of a cake baker in Equestria. <br /> <br /> Nothing wrong hurting fun there, but when things complicate a pc's life, they get beats in return (just like they would for being blind, or one handed, or wanted by the FBI, or whatever other complication one cares to come up with), they don't pay points for the privilege.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T03:28:26-07:00","id":480043,"title":"","content":"The spells are really cool. I do have a problem understanding how Crusader's current first dot works from an IC perspective. I also agree that maybe the throat cut (love it!) would made for a better first dot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T03:43:03-07:00","id":480047,"title":"","content":"@MachineIV: Thanks for answering<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=479823#post479823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering that the lancea practices would disgust the vast majority of human stigmatics, and that the benefit is essentially being the pig who is too tasty to eat all at once, the answer I'd come with is &quot;Hell to the !##$$# no.&quot;<br /> <br /> Being a human stigmatic is Grade A premium nightmare fuel territory- being locked in a closet, blood bound, or dominated into being a human ant so that some vampires who make ISIS look like nice moderates rain death, torment, and corruption on one's loved ones. Pass, thank you.<br /> <br /> Now if Stigmatics had, or could buy lancea status, to show that the lancea see them as holy vessels worthy of respect and cooperation, that would be a merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I am going with implications, but a mortal developing the wounds of Christ is not something you want to fuck with as a Sanctified. I have quite the opposite vision to yours. A stigmatic is set for life because nothing in the World of Darkness (mundane or supernatural) will get a chance to cramp their style while their undead benefactors are around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T03:43:21-07:00","id":480048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=480031#post480031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To a human stigmatic, there's no benefit, just an existence that makes the future of an expert in ancient and obscure languages in a call of cthulhu game seem as cheery as that of a cake baker in Equestria.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you <i>seen</i> the muffin makers in Starlight Glimmer's little utopia?!<br /> <br /> But on the issue of the merit it may work better as some form of upgrade to the Retainer merit? So the Kindred purchases a Retainer and pays an extra to make the mortal retainer (or Ghoul?) into a Stigmatic (but not that <i>other</i> kind of Stigmatic)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T16:22:38-07:00","id":480851,"title":"","content":"For what its worth, I really like the rituals, specially love Apple of Eden, even though I renamed it Pome of Eden for aesthetic reasons (Even if it doesn't make it to book, I'm using it!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T18:09:16-07:00","id":480960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=480851#post480851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what its worth, I really like the rituals, specially love Apple of Eden, even though I renamed it Pome of Eden for aesthetic reasons (Even if it doesn't make it to book, I'm using it!).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perhaps pomme de paradis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T18:39:41-07:00","id":480991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=480010#post480010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was definitely considered. I love the Septemi. They're one of my favorite bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Crusade reminds me of that Invictus Fighting Style in that it sort of works the same theme into a merit rather than a bloodline, which is sorta neat.<br /> <br /> Out of curiousity, are you thinking about stuff like that to sort of re-imagine these bloodlines as cultures within the Covenants? Or is there any other insight that can be offered into the concept of Crusade?<br /> <br /> I enjoy having more material to work with that makes Theban Sorcery awe-some in the classic sense. You can see why the Sanctified have become such a global phenomenon with their doctrine and the potential power of Theban Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T18:21:10-07:00","id":481799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=480960#post480960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Perhaps pomme de paradis?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds nice but not going for the french angle, just going for &quot;pome&quot; as an unspecified fruit to keep the mystery... I like the look and particulars of the medlar, which has to kind of spoil to be edible. The Fruit of Knowledge hanged in the tree a while before it was eaten, after all... And all the metaphysical stuff and stuff...<br /> <br /> And also, I like &quot;Eden&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T18:58:01-07:00","id":481818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=480991#post480991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Crusade reminds me of that Invictus Fighting Style in that it sort of works the same theme into a merit rather than a bloodline, which is sorta neat.<br /> <br /> Out of curiousity, are you thinking about stuff like that to sort of re-imagine these bloodlines as cultures within the Covenants? Or is there any other insight that can be offered into the concept of Crusade?<br /> <br /> I enjoy having more material to work with that makes Theban Sorcery awe-some in the classic sense. You can see why the Sanctified have become such a global phenomenon with their doctrine and the potential power of Theban Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to. I'd like to work a little with some of the old bloodline concepts, and blend them into more cultural elements. Just have to find time and space. <br /> <br /> Honestly, there wasn't much more to Crusade. I toyed with a playtest concept for a sort of Theban Eunuch paladin type, and I wrote something that fit it. I toyed around with that Merit a bit, and included it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T21:13:25-07:00","id":481903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=481818#post481818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to. I'd like to work a little with some of the old bloodline concepts, and blend them into more cultural elements. Just have to find time and space.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really good to hear. I think a lot of 1e bloodlines, while really interesting, would have worked better as subcultures or organizations than as bloodlines. I'd be very happy to see elements of some of those bloodlines brought back in 2e in new ways, preferably that are open to characters of different Clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T22:11:30-07:00","id":481938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=481818#post481818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wanted to. I'd like to work a little with some of the old bloodline concepts, and blend them into more cultural elements. Just have to find time and space.<br /> <br /> Honestly, there wasn't much more to Crusade. I toyed with a playtest concept for a sort of Theban Eunuch paladin type, and I wrote something that fit it. I toyed around with that Merit a bit, and included it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see the first dot of Crusade being an excellent two dot Theban Sorcery Ritual. Why not make the sacrament ones genitalia, with the proviso that it can't be healed until ones task (set upon undertaking the ritual) is complete?<br /> <br /> Effects include perhaps subtracting Theban Sorcery dots from hostile sorcery and spells or the ability to <i>parry</i> hostile spells or soceries with Weaponry, giving up or using your Action for the turn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T22:15:29-07:00","id":481942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilboD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=481938#post481938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could see the first dot of Crusade being an excellent two dot Theban Sorcery Ritual. <i>Why not make the sacrament ones genitalia</i>, with the proviso that it can't be healed until ones task (set upon undertaking the ritual) is complete?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ouch! Why would you even think of that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T07:48:57-07:00","id":483532,"title":"","content":"One thing that felt lacking from 1e is a way to steal the secrets of other covenants like Theban Sorcery or the Coils, now I'm seeing stuff that might let that happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T10:15:36-07:00","id":483694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilboD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=481938#post481938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could see the first dot of Crusade being an excellent two dot Theban Sorcery Ritual. Why not make the sacrament ones genitalia, with the proviso that it can't be healed until ones task (set upon undertaking the ritual) is complete?<br /> <br /> Effects include perhaps subtracting Theban Sorcery dots from hostile sorcery and spells or the ability to <i>parry</i> hostile spells or soceries with Weaponry, giving up or using your Action for the turn?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure he meant eunuch in the older sense of the word, meaning impotent or celibate. A Theban Eunuch would then be someone who is incapable of performing Theban Sorcery (or possibly sworn not to use it), not literally a Theban Sorcerer who has been castrated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T10:17:59-07:00","id":483695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=481942#post481942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ouch! Why would you even think of that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's the literal meaning of the word eunuch - a man who has been castrated, usually at a young enough age to have significant impact on hormonal development. Somehow I don't think that's what David meant by &quot;Theban Eunuch&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T10:53:29-07:00","id":483712,"title":"","content":"Okay, feedback time! Some of my thoughts!<br /> <br /> <b>Crusade </b>- I join the Weaponry Dots Feels Weird Chorus, but for slightly different reason. Its is that I don't like seeing it restricted to Weaponry - guns, archers, and claw-brawlers shouldn't be entirely dismissed from benefiting. I would suggest personally turn it from Weaponry to &quot;Dots in Crusade&quot; or &quot;Crusade + Status, capped at 5&quot; or something else more generic with the other vampires. That gives it a more of a faith-based, spiritual discipline feel to it, I think. Or go with &quot;appropriate physical skill.&quot;<br /> <br /> I would like to point out that I'm at a bit of a loss at its use during a vampire game. The first dot is practically limited to Cruac or fellow Thebans (Belial heretics!) - I don't see how it can apply to Ordo Coils/Scales, which should be a thing, as well as potentially the Oaths and Law. Same with the third dot - extended disciplines aren't exactly common in a combat situation, and introducing any combat tends to disrupt them. All the disciplines are all Instant or Reflexive activations, even if some of them require set up.<br /> <br /> It feels like it just doesn't work against everything except Cruac and Theban. Even the Strix and VII, major antagonists, don't offer much in the way of sorcery used against the vampires. All the other covenant Fighting Styles relied the character acting certain ways. This relies on specific antagonists being chosen. So, short of hunting the Circle or the occasional heretic plot, this just sits, which I think is a shame.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Flock </b>-A better herd merit. The willpower bit of the herd is strange, since we have no mechanics for the Herd doing anything; I was under the impression that was Retainer. There's also the question of how it interacts with Lorekeeper. Does buying Library qualify as Herd dots for purposes of buying Flock? Unsure of the mechanics behind this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Laity</b> - Okay, similar to other covenants. Moving on.<br /> <br /> <b>Sanctuary - </b>A curious twist on the old tradition. Its reactive, where you'd need to buy it as a crime happens. The merit assumes that the criminal is going to behave, however. Is that your intent? That they be good little souls and not try to sneak out like rebellious teenagers, and the like? I'm almost thinking that it might be better if the character is maintaining a Temple? Traditionally, you take refuge on holy ground; at least, that's the pop culture reference, not someone else's home that I'm familiar with.<br /> <br /> <b>Stigmata</b> - Unsure as to the timing of the bleeding here. Are we talking about set times, where you can plan it out on every Sunday and Tuesday? Does the willpower mean you're forcing it beyond the usual dots-per-week? Or just when it bleeds on what day? Feels like an alternative to the Undead Mense merit in the core book. Cool for the Lance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Temple of Damnation</b> - Holy, this is interesting. I especially like the ranged Theban bit. Its a very sexy merit that I would adore to have in any game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Apple of Eden</b> - Fun little ritual, not sure what everyone is saying its a powerful effect. Its essentially a plot hook for dealing with NPCs. I especially like the potential to use it for scaring people with wrath of god type stuff. I suppose you could say its powerful if you have a rank mortal in your game, but that's not the norm in my experience. Unless the merit is meant to work on ghouls as well as regular mortals? I am used to thinking of ghouls as not-mortals.<br /> <br /> <b>Marian Apparition - </b> Am I the only one that finds it odd that we have a visit from Mary in the Lance? Putting aside the whole Vampire-Catholic connection thing I thought the Lance moved away from, wouldn't Livian be a more appropriate image here? It feels tied into the Livian Heresy, with that Cruac benefit. Are you using Mary so other vampires can excuse the ritual with that reason, while still denouncing Livian?<br /> <br /> Another mechanics question - how do you contest an extended roll when the ritual is already complete? Normally, you contest it as the rolls are made, no? An equal number of rolls to the original rolls? Compare at the end when we hit target numbers? How does that compare to a single roll? Or is it like the new Cruac rituals where you prep before hand, then execute another roll when activated?<br /> <br /> <b>Relevatory Shroud - </b>Has a lot of overlap with Auspex 3, though it is different.<br /> <br /> <b>Apparition of the Host</b> - Now that's fun! Reminds me a bit of the old attacking owl ritual.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloody Icon</b> - I flat out hate Humanity as a cost, especially with Theban needing higher humanity for their magic. I was under the impression of Cruac users being heavy into low humanity, and Lance vamps into accumulating lots of banes.<br /> <br /> <b>Walls of Jericho -</b> While I like the effect, the low humanity requirement is very odd to me, and feels against what I thought the Lance was growing towards, thematically. The ritual says you can't have above 3 to cast it as a level 2 ritual. You need higher ratings of Theban in order to make it work. That's mind boggling. As well, I don't know if I like the variable cost, forcing you to keep a low humanity to cast a ritual like this, where as Theban as a whole needs higher Humanity to learn. I am not a fan of the odd requirements here.<br /> <br /> <b>Aaron's Rod </b>- Fun times. Lots of potential, and the combination with Animalism has some yummy possibilities.<br /> <br /> <b>Miracle of the Dead Sun - </b>Another Sacrifice-Humanity one. Again, not a fan.<br /> <br /> <b>Pledge of the Worthless One</b> - Yay Belial! What's not to love? Actually, I'm liking the idea of more &quot;heretic rituals&quot; for the different heresies. Livian, now Belial...<br /> <br /> <b>Great Prophesy -</b> Lots of potential interesting effects. Reality writing at its finest.<br /> <br /> <b>Guiding Star - </b>More catholic-christian imagery. I wonder if a level 4 ritual for what amounts to a safe haven for a night is a bit high.<br /> <br /> <b>Apocalypse</b> - Break the Masquerade!<br /> <br /> <b>Judgement Fast</b> - Judgement on the city, which is painful for Elders that are running around. Very neat and powerful for the Lance moving to take command.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There's two things I notice with the rituals. A lot of love for heretical spells here, which is wildly awesome. Says a lot about the covenant and Theban as a whole. The second is there seems to be a comeback of &quot;sacrifice your humanity&quot; themes, which I feel is at odds with core book descriptions of Theban. I suspect that might be the reason, a whole &quot;sacrifice what's most precious to you for desperate times,&quot; but I feel like its way over cost. Or establishing some kind of Sanctity rule for using it this way.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to see some more Jewish and Islamic symbolism in some of the rituals instead of predominantly christian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-17-2015, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T10:57:09-07:00","id":483728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=481818#post481818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wanted to. I'd like to work a little with some of the old bloodline concepts, and blend them into more cultural elements. Just have to find time and space.<br /> <br /> Honestly, there wasn't much more to Crusade. I toyed with a playtest concept for a sort of Theban Eunuch paladin type, and I wrote something that fit it. I toyed around with that Merit a bit, and included it.</div> </div> </div> </div> I do like that idea. Its execution, with Crusade, leaves a bit desired. The Septimi, the dragon-monks, a few theban rituals that did similar things... they all were broader than what Crusade does. That's part of my issue. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T14:16:49-07:00","id":483885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=483695#post483695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the literal meaning of the word eunuch - a man who has been castrated, usually at a young enough age to have significant impact on hormonal development. Somehow I don't think that's what David meant by &quot;Theban Eunuch&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I definitely understand the distinctions and nuances of the word &quot;eunuch&quot;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, and knew David's original meaning to be more metaphorical. However, given some vampire powers and blood magic require actual gruesome sacrifice of body parts or worse, I believed poster GilboD's suggestion was referring to literal castration for it's thematic elements (a condition not nearly as dire or permanent to the undead). My comment was also made entirely in jest. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T14:41:10-07:00","id":483901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=483712#post483712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Crusade </b>- <br /> I would like to point out that I'm at a bit of a loss at its use during a vampire game. The first dot is practically limited to Cruac or fellow Thebans (Belial heretics!) - I don't see how it can apply to Ordo Coils/Scales, which should be a thing, as well as potentially the Oaths and Law. Same with the third dot - extended disciplines aren't exactly common in a combat situation, and introducing any combat tends to disrupt them. All the disciplines are all Instant or Reflexive activations, even if some of them require set up.<br /> <br /> It feels like it just doesn't work against everything except Cruac and Theban. Even the Strix and VII, major antagonists, don't offer much in the way of sorcery used against the vampires. All the other covenant Fighting Styles relied the character acting certain ways. This relies on specific antagonists being chosen. So, short of hunting the Circle or the occasional heretic plot, this just sits, which I think is a shame.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the intention of Crusade, at least in part, is to provide combat enhancement when dealing with other supernatural beings that pose a threat to vampires. Crusade not only has value against vampiric users of blood magic like TS and Cruac, but also against the Arcana of mages, Gifts of werewolves, Contract of changelings, etc. <br /> <br /> I personally have no objection to abilities that are more applicable to the wider nWOD, particularly since crossover is not uncommon, other templates benefit from similar rules withing their games lines, and OPP is implicitly encouraging more crossover with games like Beast. Nevertheless, as I indicated earlier, Crusade does need some noticeable tweaking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Flock </b>-A better herd merit. The willpower bit of the herd is strange, since we have no mechanics for the Herd doing anything; I was under the impression that was Retainer. There's also the question of how it interacts with Lorekeeper. Does buying Library qualify as Herd dots for purposes of buying Flock? Unsure of the mechanics behind this. </div> </div> </div>I like the willpower dot benefit. To me, in represents a Herd that it truly motivated, loyal and proactive, without being too powerful or stepping on the toes of other merits such as Retainer or Allies<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Apple of Eden</b> - Fun little ritual, not sure what everyone is saying its a powerful effect. Its essentially a plot hook for dealing with NPCs. I especially like the potential to use it for scaring people with wrath of god type stuff. I suppose you could say its powerful if you have a rank mortal in your game, but that's not the norm in my experience. Unless the merit is meant to work on ghouls as well as regular mortals? I am used to thinking of ghouls as not-mortals. </div> </div> </div>I, too, like this ritual, but am still very curious if &quot;being able to see supernatural creatures for what they are&quot; provides the recipient any protection against werewolf Lunacy or the Quiescence from Mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Bloody Icon</b> - I flat out hate Humanity as a cost, especially with Theban needing higher humanity for their magic. I was under the impression of Cruac users being heavy into low humanity, and Lance vamps into accumulating lots of banes.<br /> <br /> <b>Miracle of the Dead Sun - </b>Another Sacrifice-Humanity one. Again, not a fan. </div> </div> </div>I like the Humanity cost. Significant powers require a significant price, and they maintain the martyr elements of the Lancea et Sanctum. They actually remind me of powerful Goblin Contracts from Changeling. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's two things I notice with the rituals. A lot of love for heretical spells here, which is wildly awesome. Says a lot about the covenant and Theban as a whole. The second is there seems to be a comeback of &quot;sacrifice your humanity&quot; themes, which I feel is at odds with core book descriptions of Theban. I suspect that might be the reason, a whole &quot;sacrifice what's most precious to you for desperate times,&quot; but I feel like its way over cost. Or establishing some kind of Sanctity rule for using it this way.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to see some more Jewish and Islamic symbolism in some of the rituals instead of predominantly christian. </div> </div> </div>I couldn't possibly agree more. Adding &quot;heretical&quot; spells subtly challenges the very essence of the LeS in a fun way. I would also welcome rituals with Jewish, Islamic and other non-Christian iconography, both for their &quot;heretical&quot; aspects, and because it might encourage some players who are uncomfortable with the heavy Catholic themes to experiment and play characters associated with the Covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T10:06:03-07:00","id":484680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=483901#post483901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the intention of Crusade, at least in part, is to provide combat enhancement when dealing with other supernatural beings that pose a threat to vampires. Crusade not only has value against vampiric users of blood magic like TS and Cruac, but also against the Arcana of mages, Gifts of werewolves, Contract of changelings, etc.<br /> <br /> I personally have no objection to abilities that are more applicable to the wider nWOD, particularly since crossover is not uncommon, other templates benefit from similar rules withing their games lines, and OPP is implicitly encouraging more crossover with games like Beast. Nevertheless, as I indicated earlier, Crusade does need some noticeable tweaking.</div> </div> </div> </div> I get the crossover stuff, but I think that's more of a &quot;Oh, sure, use this stuff outside of vampire stuff easily!&quot; I don't think its the main thrust of the FS. From inside a pure vampire game standpoint, I'd like to see it more applicable against the Strix and other covenants than the Circle and Lance, most notably VII. As it stands, I believe its pretty much limited to Crones, Lances, and the occasional strix who knows Cruac.<br /> <br /> First dot and third dot only apply to &quot;incoming spells, rituals, or sorceries.&quot; That's blood magic (Theban and Cruac only), werewolf rites, Awakened magic, some hunter Endowments. Prommies have no equivalent. Changeling and Demons make tokens/gadgets and use pledges/pacts as the closest equivalent for their &quot;ritual magic.&quot; Sin-Eater Ceremonies aren't offensive - only two target non-ghost people and both are beneficial. That ignores four of six covenants, a good chunk of the strix, and four of the eight other games (two of which have non-offensive sorceries). Effectively, that means Acolytes, fellow Lance, some Cruac-using strix, mages, and half of tier 3 Hunters out of the whole WoD.<br /> <br /> Well, the second dot is widely applicable against anyone who's power requires speech, but that's just cutting off High Speech, Dominate, and the two or three Unchained vocal powers as far as I know. Maybe Mummy Utterances, not as familiar enough to know if that's a literal utterance required. Again, kind of limited.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like the willpower dot benefit. To me, in represents a Herd that it truly motivated, loyal and proactive, without being too powerful or stepping on the toes of other merits such as Retainer or Allies </div> </div> </div> My point wasn't about liking or not liking. Its about how the rules works in execution. How does the mechanics behind it work? I don't think that's clear enough. Do we assume 2 rating in everything? Just the three dice from spending the willpower? How many people make up the herd, and how many points of willpower is that? What types of situation would it involve? Would they attack if their faith required it? Is it just used to resist something?<br /> <br /> I like the idea, I just don't know how that willpower would work in game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like the Humanity cost. Significant powers require a significant price, and they maintain the martyr elements of the Lancea et Sanctum. They actually remind me of powerful Goblin Contracts from Changeling. </div> </div> </div> While it looks cool on paper, in execution I never see them used. And that's the fundamental issue I have. Most players I know avoid investing in the Contracts of Sacrifice. While they're strong, they effectively require exp investments not only to buy the power, but again once a PC uses it. There was one or two Lance rituals that sacrificed Humanity before, and I don't recall ever seeing anyone buy or use them either.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I couldn't possibly agree more. Adding &quot;heretical&quot; spells subtly challenges the very essence of the LeS in a fun way. I would also welcome rituals with Jewish, Islamic and other non-Christian iconography, both for their &quot;heretical&quot; aspects, and because it might encourage some players who are uncomfortable with the heavy Catholic themes to experiment and play characters associated with the Covenant. </div> </div> </div> The mere fact that you are saying that the jewish- and islamic-based creeds have heretical aspects, even if joking, are the main reason I think we need more of them. They're not heresies, they're mainstream Lance religions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-18-2015, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T11:18:41-07:00","id":484755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=483712#post483712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels like it just doesn't work against everything except Cruac and Theban. Even the Strix and VII, major antagonists, don't offer much in the way of sorcery used against the vampires. All the other covenant Fighting Styles relied the character acting certain ways. This relies on specific antagonists being chosen. So, short of hunting the Circle or the occasional heretic plot, this just sits, which I think is a shame.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I have to agree with. As I mentioned before, Cruac and Theban rituals take generally somewhere between 15 minutes and an hour to do, they're not something you're going to break out in the middle of combat. Then, rituals are already considered a failure if they're interrupted, so you're not just having to find the ritual being enacted, you're going to have to not interrupt it before your big attack. Which leads us to the big attack itself. People performing a ritual have no defense, which is great for the Crusader, but they're using a willpower and still attacking at a -2 penalty. I think, given the cost and that the targets, until we get some further combat ritualists, it would make more sense for the penalty to be gone, or even the Willpower point to help out with the roll. I prefer the latter, with their zeal helping them make the attack.<br /> <br /> But then you get to the repercussions, and you've done some extra damage which is probably bashing, and turned a failure into a dramatic failure for them. But what does a dramatic failure do for a ritualist? In both cases of blood sorcery, you get a penalty to your next ritual, but if the ritual is that of Theban sorcery, they get the Humbled condition, which gives them a penalty to their Resolve rolls and makes them unable to gain Willpower through their Requiem. This can be pretty good, even the description seems appropriate, 'Your character has felt the touch fo the divine and trembled. She feels unworthy and wretched.' But if you look at Cruac if you get the dramatic failure you're hit with the Tempted condition, which gives you a penalty to resist Frenzy, making the attack somewhat like poking a bear, since Frenzying vampires can be very dangerous. Looking over at Werewolf, you get the Shadowlash condition, which gives you a penalty to interacting with Spirits and the Shadow, certainly not as dangerous as a frenzying vampire but low in payout for the Crusader.<br /> <br /> I think the problems lie in its limited use, and its cost for potentially low payoff. I have no idea what to do for the limited use, but there may be rituals more likely to be used in combat as time goes by and mage or other games come out. Or further books might have extended Disciplines. For the investment, which isn't exactly high but does require 3 Merits and a lot in the way of prerequisites, I think changing how the willpower cost works would be a nice step. But the big thing would be the Dramatic Failure. I think it would be thematically and mechanically more advantageous if instead of this it should simply afflict the Humbled condition, or a variant that allowed for other supernaturals, since Vampires are so far the only ones gaining Willpower through Requiems and Masks.<br /> <br /> I dig the rest, though. I especially like the idea of the Flock, Temple and Sanctuary merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-18-2015, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T14:39:16-07:00","id":484850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=484680#post484680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I get the crossover stuff, but I think that's more of a &quot;Oh, sure, use this stuff outside of vampire stuff easily!&quot; I don't think its the main thrust of the FS. From inside a pure vampire game standpoint, I'd like to see it more applicable against the Strix and other covenants than the Circle and Lance, most notably VII. As it stands, I believe its pretty much limited to Crones, Lances, and the occasional strix who knows Cruac.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a major part of the problem is the difficultly of doing what you suggest with just a fighting style merit, even if ostensibly mystically based, without effectively turning it into a vampire discipline or set of devotions, requiring prerequisite dots of Theban Sorcery, or thematically stepping on the toes of bloodlines like the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/\" target=\"_blank\">Khabait</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mere fact that you are saying that the jewish- and islamic-based creeds have heretical aspects, even if joking, are the main reason I think we need more of them. They're not heresies, they're mainstream Lance religions. </div> </div> </div>The non-Catholic LeS creeds seem to appear more on paper than actually evident in the setting. We certainly agree that adding some rituals with non-Catholic iconography would certainly help dispel this issue.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T02:12:55-07:00","id":485229,"title":"","content":"Then again adding several religious doctrines within one covenant dilutes the whole covenants theme. Lancea et Sanctum has a strong theme as catholic Vampires adding Islam, Judaism and Scientology etc. there works only to dilute that theme and thus the covenant as a whole.<br /> <br /> I'd rather stick with a strong theme and keep the Covenant as Catholics only, converting Vampires aggressively when needed, than dilute that theme by including every possible religion.<br /> <br /> Muslim Vampires, I think, would rather make their own Covenant than join/share one with Catholic Vampires. Thus instead of messing up the LeS just find the word-count somewhere, likely a region book of some sort or a type of Dark Era, to add a new Islamic Covenant with it's own views of Vampirism. Similar should be done with other religions as well as if there is something to be learned from the real world it is that different religions do not mix. Forcing Islam into LeS sounds like a similar idea to trying to force Islam to join the Catholic Church, not likely to happen. Deeply religious people often have a hard time accepting that others believe differently, this is likely even more pronounced with vampires, and thus such mixed covenant doesn't sound plausible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T03:27:02-07:00","id":485236,"title":"","content":"That is actually a thing already. The Banu Shaitan are the Muslim equivalent of the L+S. They have gotten some word count in Ancient Mysteries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T05:42:50-07:00","id":485353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=484850#post484850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a major part of the problem is the difficultly of doing what you suggest with just a fighting style merit, even if ostensibly mystically based, without effectively turning it into a vampire discipline or set of devotions, requiring prerequisite dots of Theban Sorcery, or thematically stepping on the toes of bloodlines like the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/\" target=\"_blank\">Khabait</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, Mr Hill suggested that its slightly based on the Septimi, who in turn have things in common with a few Theban rituals and the Mehket Dragon-monk bloodline. In all three cases, we have such powers that affect disciplines as well as sorceries, making them widely applicable. I think that, if we have the new Invictus FS able to hurt people with words, its possible to have a bit more flexible FS.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The non-Catholic LeS creeds seem to appear more on paper than actually evident in the setting. We certainly agree that adding some rituals with non-Catholic iconography would certainly help dispel this issue. </div> </div> </div> Agreed. The entire Mary references alone kinda makes me raise an eyebrow for this reason. Its so blindingly obviously Catholic. Not even vampire-religion-with-hints-of-Catholic, we're talking flat out Catholic. The Lance is supposed to be its own entity, where Jesus arguably doesn't matter, then we get things like this.<br /> <br /> I get, and do like, the Livian Heresy potential, but I don't know if referencing Mary in the write up is ideal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=485229#post485229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again adding several religious doctrines within one covenant dilutes the whole covenants theme. Lancea et Sanctum has a strong theme as catholic Vampires adding Islam, Judaism and Scientology etc. there works only to dilute that theme and thus the covenant as a whole.<br /> <br /> I'd rather stick with a strong theme and keep the Covenant as Catholics only, converting Vampires aggressively when needed, than dilute that theme by including every possible religion.</div> </div> </div> </div> Check the Lancea Sanctum book. Despite the Catholic vibe, there's supposed to be Jewish, Muslim, Baptist, Orthodox, and other Abrahamic Creeds within the Lancea Sanctum since the covenant came out ten years ago. We're not diluting anything that's not already there. Look up the Dammatic, Iblic, Monachal, Westminster, and Tollison creed. These are the five major creeds touched on in the Lance book. And that's before we start touching on the heresies.<br /> <br /> The problem is that we've never been given <i>support</i> for these Creeds, and the impression of the L+S being entirely Catholic has grown. A call for supporting these other faiths within the L+S is certainly something I think needs to happen. The Lance, throughout 1e, has suffered under a tunnel vision. 2e needs to break out and expand the Lance in a wide variety of ways.<br /> <br /> The Invictus isn't just a giant boardroom of corporate sharks. Why should the Lance be forced under a single mold? That's actively harmful to the game as a whole. Diversity can only help the game going forwards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Muslim Vampires, I think, would rather make their own Covenant than join/share one with Catholic Vampires. Thus instead of messing up the LeS just find the word-count somewhere, likely a region book of some sort or a type of Dark Era, to add a new Islamic Covenant with it's own views of Vampirism. Similar should be done with other religions as well as if there is something to be learned from the real world it is that different religions do not mix. Forcing Islam into LeS sounds like a similar idea to trying to force Islam to join the Catholic Church, not likely to happen. Deeply religious people often have a hard time accepting that others believe differently, this is likely even more pronounced with vampires, and thus such mixed covenant doesn't sound plausible. </div> </div> </div> The Circle of the Crone would like some words with you about mixed religions not getting along in a game setting. And you're acting like internal divisions over ideals or philosophy have never troubled a covenant before. And, frankly, such divisions are actually within theme for such a religious covenant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> One of the goals of the writers, it seems to me, is embracing cultural diversity within the game. Asking for that to be reflected in the writeup, rituals, and merits of the Lance shouldn't be too much to ask for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-19-2015, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T07:19:28-07:00","id":485390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=485353#post485353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The entire Mary references alone kinda makes me raise an eyebrow for this reason. Its so blindingly obviously Catholic. Not even vampire-religion-with-hints-of-Catholic, we're talking flat out Catholic. The Lance is supposed to be its own entity, where Jesus arguably doesn't matter, then we get things like this.<br /> <br /> I get, and do like, the Livian Heresy potential, but I don't know if referencing Mary in the write up is ideal.<br /> <br /> Check the Lancea Sanctum book. Despite the Catholic vibe, there's supposed to be Jewish, Muslim, Baptist, Orthodox, and other Abrahamic Creeds within the Lancea Sanctum since the covenant came out ten years ago. We're not diluting anything that's not already there. Look up the Dammatic, Iblic, Monachal, Westminster, and Tollison creed. These are the five major creeds touched on in the Lance book. And that's before we start touching on the heresies.<br /> <br /> The problem is that we've never been given <i>support</i> for these Creeds, and the impression of the L+S being entirely Catholic has grown. A call for supporting these other faiths within the L+S is certainly something I think needs to happen. The Lance, throughout 1e, has suffered under a tunnel vision. 2e needs to break out and expand the Lance in a wide variety of ways.<br /> <br /> The Invictus isn't just a giant boardroom of corporate sharks. Why should the Lance be forced under a single mold? That's actively harmful to the game as a whole. Diversity can only help the game going forwards.<br /> <br /> The Circle of the Crone would like some words with you about mixed religions not getting along in a game setting. And you're acting like internal divisions over ideals or philosophy have never troubled a covenant before. And, frankly, such divisions are actually within theme for such a religious covenant.<br /> <br /> One of the goals of the writers, it seems to me, is embracing cultural diversity within the game. Asking for that to be reflected in the writeup, rituals, and merits of the Lance shouldn't be too much to ask for.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, the Cruac side effect of the Marian Apparition ritual hints that Theban sorcery is intrinsically neither Longinian nor Christian. In practice, most Spears follow Catholic traditions. I suspect that if the right pagan sorcerer used that ritual (or another interpretation of it), a different woman appear, possibly a goddess. The ritual could be particularly interesting where the Blood-Blessed from <i>Requiem for Regina </i>are concerned or its successors in the 19th century that I speculate created the Circle of the Crone in Ireland.<br /> <br /> I think <i>Blood and Smoke</i>'s way of presenting cultural diversity is to present covenants outside the big five, which have Western emphases <i>because that's where they come from</i>. Particularly in the Asian sample cities, we see covenants like the big five with unrelated origins. For example, 1E Tokyo an Invictus stronghold; in 2E, it still is a giant boardroom of corporate sharks, but they're not Invictus and the old Ventrue empire wasn't called Invictus either. The Circle of the Crone was only mentioned in the three North American cities and two Western European ones. While the Circle of the Crone does absorb vampires who followed their religions before the movement's inception, there will be some pagan vampires who want nothing to do with them and some who have never encountered them.<br /> <br /> Going back to <i>Requiem for Regina</i>, it does mention the Westminster Creed and the Icarians. It even mentions Invictus in the Far East. So there might be more that approach to come. However, it also mentions three faiths connected to Christianity, but not the Lancea et Sanctum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 04-19-2015, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T07:33:25-07:00","id":485395,"title":"","content":"I've gotten the impression that the Lancea et Sanctum is no longer so all encompassing as to include Jewish and Islamic sects (from their 2e core writeup), which seems fine by me since I'd much rather those have their own covenants, rather than just folding all of it in under the umbrella of the Sanctified. I think that was a consequence of how they wrote the Covenants in 1e, and something that can be repaired in the 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> That said, I think they don't want people to think of them as Catholic. It seems like they're willing to defend the Catholic flock, but their rituals are different enough that they basically only share a superficial, aesthetic similarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 04-19-2015, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T08:28:22-07:00","id":485428,"title":"","content":"Despite giving lip-service to inclusion of other faiths, the L+S are pretty clearly only Christian. They especially CANNOT include Muslims. I usually explain it this way: you're a Christian vampire and you discover the L+S. You can fully convert to the L+S without breaking any of your previous beliefs. <br /> If you're a Muslim though? Islam is predicated upon it being the capstone of Abrahamic faiths. If you convert to the L+S as a Muslim, you first have to deny that the Qur'an overwrote previous texts, and additionally accept that Jesus was more than a Prophet (albeit one of the handful of most elite prophets). In doing so, you have to stop becoming a Muslim BEFORE you become a Longinian. It also includes way more details that are key to the Longinian story that denied in Islam: Jesus didn't die on the cross, for example. So you'd have to a) deny that Muhammad was the Seal of the Prophets, as his prophecies should override Longinus', and b) deny that Jesus was uplifted from the cross alive into heaven, and thus deny that the word of the Qur'an is the word of God. At that point, most Muslims of most beliefs would say you are no longer a Muslim, and have committed apostasy. <br /> Thus, L+S CAN'T include Muslims, but rather it can include ex-Muslims. <br /> <br /> Judaism as well has issues, mostly with accepting Jesus as a Prophet, as according to Talmudic Law, no prophet can contradict previous prophets as Jesus does. It's not as huge an issue, however, as the above ones. <br /> <br /> But yeah, it's better to stop pretending that L+S are accepting of all monotheistic faiths, and accept that L+S are the pseudo-Christian covenant. As it relates to Marinian Apparition (which I keep expecting to be Marius, reading it as Marian Apparition, oops), I think that the focus on Mary is off, as others have said. L+S work best, for me, when they're PARALLEL to Christianity, not fully part of Christianity. They feed of Christian traditions, so they very well may feed off apparitions of the Judgemental Female Figure, but it being specifically Mary strikes me as very much &quot;Catholics are Right and Protestants are Wrong&quot;. Perhaps making the figure fuzzy, making it obviously female, radiating holiness and judginess, would be better than making it be identifiable as a specific figure. Then Catholic-leaning vampires can say it's Mary or Livia, Protestant vampires can say it's Livia or just a holy apparition of the Judgemental Female Figure, while Crone followers can say its the Dark Mother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T08:43:36-07:00","id":485433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=485395#post485395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've gotten the impression that the Lancea et Sanctum is no longer so all encompassing as to include Jewish and Islamic sects (from their 2e core writeup), which seems fine by me since I'd much rather those have their own covenants, rather than just folding all of it in under the umbrella of the Sanctified. I think that was a consequence of how they wrote the Covenants in 1e, and something that can be repaired in the 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> That said, I think they don't want people to think of them as Catholic. It seems like they're willing to defend the Catholic flock, but their rituals are different enough that they basically only share a superficial, aesthetic similarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well 2E already went against that archetype with superficially non-conformist Sanctified. I think the idea is that their fundamental faith isn't Christian, but they pick up Christian traditions and sometimes those of other religions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 04-19-2015, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T09:19:56-07:00","id":485453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Check the Lancea Sanctum book. Despite the Catholic vibe, there's supposed to be Jewish, Muslim, Baptist, Orthodox, and other Abrahamic Creeds within the Lancea Sanctum since the covenant came out ten years ago. We're not diluting anything that's not already there. Look up the Dammatic, Iblic, Monachal, Westminster, and Tollison creed. These are the five major creeds touched on in the Lance book. And that's before we start touching on the heresies. </div> </div> </div>That's 1st Edition and I admit not being that familiar with it but it is also something I did not get, at all, from the B&amp;S description of LeS and I frankly prefer the latter. WW did this kinda mess with Celestial Chorus of cWoD's Mage and in my opinion trying to group all religions under one banner was a mistake then and it still is now. With B&amp;S we have the opportunity to correct messes like this and it is what should be done here, keep LeS as parallel to Christianity and make the other religions have their own appropriate Covenants instead of muddying the one we have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T09:45:18-07:00","id":485459,"title":"","content":"While I haven't really read the L&amp;S Covenant book, honestly, the idea of non-Christian Sanctified have never really made sense to me. The cornerstone of their faith is that Longinus was Damned by God for killing Jesus. That's kind of a hard pill to swallow if you don't believe Jesus was the son of God, or at the very least, under some kind of divine protection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T10:30:37-07:00","id":485487,"title":"","content":"They place the emphasis on them being Embraced being part of Gods plan, whoever their God may be, showing the kine the price of sin, and not the Longinus aspect.<br /> <br /> It's similar to how the Circle of the Crone was of the belief that being a vampire was a gift from the Crone and one you should embrace. Except who the Crone was could vary from place to place.<br /> <br /> Or how the Carthians promote change and revolution from the old traditions, but their methods and goals vary from coterie to coterie.<br /> <br /> Or how the Invictus believe in a hierarchy that held up tradition and respect, to a point, in their efforts to keep the Masquerade and vampires large and in charge, but they weren't all necessarily based on the neo-feudal system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-19-2015, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T10:33:02-07:00","id":485489,"title":"","content":"Wasn't Longinus just making sure he was already dead though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T10:38:03-07:00","id":485492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=485487#post485487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They place the emphasis on them being Embraced being part of Gods plan, whoever their God may be, showing the kine the price of sin, and not the Longinus aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>That just seems like a tool to ease the process of converting to Longinism. The religion is ultimately founded on Christian beliefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T10:44:11-07:00","id":485496,"title":"","content":"The Longinus part is the way to ease the process, giving them a figure to look up to. The whole system is about playing a part in traditional religion. God/Yahweh/Allah has a plan for you, you exist to show the humans the cost of sin, to help them appreciate their lives and stay on the Right Track. To aid in this, God has given you divine sorceries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T10:48:45-07:00","id":485499,"title":"","content":"I am with Charlaquin. The Iblic and Dammitic Creed never made much sense to me. Which is why I significantly prefered the idea of the Banu Shaitan as shown in Ancient Mysteries. I think it simply works better when the L+S is VAMPIRE CHRISTIANITY only and other Abrahamic faiths have their own versions independent of the Lance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T10:51:07-07:00","id":485500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=485496#post485496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Longinus part is the way to ease the process, giving them a figure to look up to. The whole system is about playing a part in traditional religion. God/Yahweh/Allah has a plan for you, you exist to show the humans the cost of sin, to help them appreciate their lives and stay on the Right Track. To aid in this, God has given you divine sorceries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but you kind of have to concede that Jesus was pretty important to that God (who ever He/She/It/They may be) if you accept the Testiment of Longinus. That could be difficult for people who belonged to non-Christian religions in life. I suppose you could theoretically join the Lance without accepting the Testiment of Longinus? Seems strange to me though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T11:03:50-07:00","id":485505,"title":"","content":"They didn't join the Lancea Sanctum. The Banu Shaitan, the Dammitics, the Exotheists, they're their own covenants, not a part of the Lancea Sanctum. So throw out any idea of them following Longinus or believing in Christ, or Christ as the son of God or whatever. They're not branches of the Lancea Sanctum. Sometimes multiple covenants exist in one city, at an uneasy peace. Often times, there's holy wars. The Banu Shaitan follow inversions of the Five Pillars of Islam, the Dammitics follow the Testament of Longinus without aspects of Jesus-as-Savior.<br /> <br /> However, when it comes down to it, they do the same thing. They share the base core beliefs of the Lancea Sanctum. They were sinners, chosen and cursed by God/Allah/Yahweh/Nothing, and now exist to test and torment humanity so they can stay on the Right Track.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T11:13:25-07:00","id":485510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=485505#post485505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They didn't join the Lancea Sanctum. The Banu Shaitan, the Dammitics, the Exotheists, they're their own covenants, not a part of the Lancea Sanctum. So throw out any idea of them following Longinus or believing in Christ, or Christ as the son of God or whatever. They're not branches of the Lancea Sanctum. Sometimes multiple covenants exist in one city, at an uneasy peace. Often times, there's holy wars. The Banu Shaitan follow inversions of the Five Pillars of Islam, the Dammitics follow the Testament of Longinus without aspects of Jesus-as-Savior.<br /> <br /> However, when it comes down to it, they do the same thing. They share the base core beliefs of the Lancea Sanctum. They were sinners, chosen and cursed by God/Allah/Yahweh/Nothing, and now exist to test and torment humanity so they can stay on the Right Track.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are clearly talking about different things here. What I said was that non-Christan Sanctified didn't make sense to me. If these groups are their own Covenants and not branches of the Lancea et Sanctum, then their members are not non-Christian members of the Lancea et Sanctum, and therefore not what I was talking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T11:13:40-07:00","id":485511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=485428#post485428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah, it's better to stop pretending that L+S are accepting of all monotheistic faiths, and accept that L+S are the pseudo-Christian covenant. As it relates to Marinian Apparition (which I keep expecting to be Marius, reading it as Marian Apparition, oops), I think that the focus on Mary is off, as others have said. L+S work best, for me, when they're PARALLEL to Christianity, not fully part of Christianity. They feed of Christian traditions, so they very well may feed off apparitions of the Judgemental Female Figure, but it being specifically Mary strikes me as very much &quot;Catholics are Right and Protestants are Wrong&quot;. Perhaps making the figure fuzzy, making it obviously female, radiating holiness and judginess, would be better than making it be identifiable as a specific figure. Then Catholic-leaning vampires can say it's Mary or Livia, Protestant vampires can say it's Livia or just a holy apparition of the Judgemental Female Figure, while Crone followers can say its the Dark Mother.</div> </div> </div> </div>She probably is fuzzy. I doubt she introduces herself. She's a pure maiden and mother and she looks into your eyes as if she see your soul. Other than that, the only thing that could identify her as Mary would be her clothes matching those you see in images of Mary. I doubt think Livia or the Dark Mother would make sense because Livia was a whore and the Dark Mother is Dark; the ritual requires a pure white sheet.<br /> If you've read <i>Shadows of the UK</i> or at least seen the Gentleman's review on Youtube, you might remember the People's Princess. The Marian Apparition could be something analogous to that or something that existed before the Virgin Mary.<br /> <br /> While I don't much care for the Lancea Sanctum's various creeds, I did quite like how the author described the African Icarians having a more Egyptian flavour, which is imposed by force in places far from Egypt; it's distinct, but true to the Lancea et Sanctum. Meanwhile, I think 2E Westminster Spears can be spun into 18th century Exotheists who abandoned the syncretism that was increasingly associated with the Blood-Blessed without actively avoiding Christianity altogether, rather than a direct Anglican version of the covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 04-19-2015, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T11:41:58-07:00","id":485523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=485459#post485459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I haven't really read the L&amp;S Covenant book, honestly, the idea of non-Christian Sanctified have never really made sense to me. The cornerstone of their faith is that Longinus was Damned by God for killing Jesus. That's kind of a hard pill to swallow if you don't believe Jesus was the son of God, or at the very least, under some kind of divine protection.</div> </div> </div> </div> Most Jewish and Islamic faithful I've talked to on the matter usually just describe Jesus as a prophet or rabbi following prophetic tradition, akin to Moses. So, yes. As far as I'm aware, saying that Jesus was under divine protection makes perfect sense in this case.<br /> <br /> A quick google search tells me that Jesus is actually mentioned in the Qu'ran as well. Not sure how accurate that is, but there you go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-19-2015, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T11:58:21-07:00","id":485530,"title":"","content":"He's considered a Prophet, but not the son of God, if I remember correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T12:11:21-07:00","id":485564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=485530#post485530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's considered a Prophet, but not the son of God, if I remember correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, not the Messiah, the Son of God, or anything like that. That I completely agree with. But the idea that Jesus was under divine protection of some kind would not be amiss in Jewish and Islamic lore, which Charlaquin said. <br /> <br /> Many Jewish are uncomfortable discussing Jesus, due to the history of prejudice, anti-semeticism and a few other factors. But I don't see how it would be a hard pill to swallow that Longinus couldn't become a vampire prophet for whatever reasons, or whatever the equivalent would be, given that the Jewish lore states that age of prophets ended before the birth of Jesus. <br /> <br /> And I don't see how there wouldn't be different translations of the Testament, some of which say Jesus was the Son of God, others which would not. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T12:34:07-07:00","id":485572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=485564#post485564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No, not the Messiah, the Son of God, or anything like that. That I completely agree with. But the idea that Jesus was under divine protection of some kind would not be amiss in Jewish and Islamic lore, which Charlaquin said. <br /> <br /> Many Jewish are uncomfortable discussing Jesus, due to the history of prejudice, anti-semeticism and a few other factors. But I don't see how it would be a hard pill to swallow that Longinus couldn't become a vampire prophet for whatever reasons, or whatever the equivalent would be, given that the Jewish lore states that age of prophets ended before the birth of Jesus. <br /> <br /> And I don't see how there wouldn't be different translations of the Testament, some of which say Jesus was the Son of God, others which would not. </div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I guess it's not out of the question. It still seems a little forced to me, but there you go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T12:39:02-07:00","id":485575,"title":"","content":"Forced or not, I don't mind which way they go. However, if they are going to drop the Benu and Iblic creeds as well as the Dammitic, then I'd like a definitive answer from the writers on the issue. It admittedly does seem that way from the new writeup, but how much of it is meant to exclude all the other books? I'm told in one thread that all the old books inform the new stuff, and are used, and in another, we have to ignore what's written before.<br /> <br /> I'd also really love to hear from someone who's actually a jew or muslim on the matter, or at least someone who's studied it in depth. A few google searches and a half-remembered comparative religion class aren't exactly enough to make me an expert here. I simply cannot say that something is or isn't forced, or that its offensive or not, if we don't have any expert voice on the matter to testify to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-19-2015, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T13:04:30-07:00","id":485604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=485575#post485575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forced or not, I don't mind which way they go. However, if they are going to drop the Benu and Iblic creeds as well as the Dammitic, then I'd like a definitive answer from the writers on the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if what nofather says is true and they are separate Covenants, not branches of the Lancea et Sanctum, then I don't see an issue. Each group can represent a vampiric take on their respective religion. If they are all branches of the Lance, I guess I just don't get why.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=485575#post485575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also really love to hear from someone who's actually a jew or muslim on the matter, or at least someone who's studied it in depth. A few google searches and a half-remembered comparative religion class aren't exactly enough to make me an expert here. I simply cannot say that something is or isn't forced, or that its offensive or not, if we don't have any expert voice on the matter to testify to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, that would definitely be helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T13:24:14-07:00","id":485610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=485604#post485604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if what nofather says is true and they are separate Covenants, not branches of the Lancea et Sanctum, then I don't see an issue. Each group can represent a vampiric take on their respective religion. If they are all branches of the Lance, I guess I just don't get why.</div> </div> </div> </div> The thing, to me, is that the &quot;default&quot; Lance that everyone thinks of is the Monochal style. You can't even do other christian style denominations from the way some people treat the Lance. Its a lot like the CotC. While, on paper, we can have different &quot;pagan&quot; religions be part of it, but in execution, we effectively have the vampire version of Wicca. It really makes it difficult to be something other than Catholic or Wiccian inside the Circle or Lance. Which is bad for the game when I want to play something different.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, that's a separate covenant!&quot; means we'd need to devise everything new from the ground up. I don't see that, especially when we seem to be getting not just the Livian Heresy built into the Lance, but Belial's Brood too. If we're folding the Brood into the Lance...<br /> <br /> EDIT - And I really don't see how what nofather says can be true. Exotheists, by definition, are Sanctified who follow Sanctified teachings as a way of life instead of a matter of faith or belief. You <i>can't</i> make them a separate covenant; they're literally defined by the L+S.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-19-2015, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T13:31:37-07:00","id":485660,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I see your point. Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T13:35:02-07:00","id":485664,"title":"","content":"You could just have the Not-Lancea et Sanctum have Totally-not-Theban-Sorcery-Honest rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T13:36:42-07:00","id":485665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=485660#post485660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... I see your point. Thank you!</div> </div> </div> </div> No, thank you. We are here, after all, to try and voice our thoughts for the writers to hear, and I enjoy having the discussion on these matters. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T16:12:19-07:00","id":485814,"title":"","content":"About Jesus, although is a very important figure on Islam (the second greatest prophet after Muhammad), it's irrelevant about Longinus. Jesus never was crucified, so Longinus killed a &quot;false&quot; Jesus, not the true prophet.<br /> <br /> <br /> About the Creeds, I don't have any problem with Dammitic Creed being part of Lancea et Sanctum. Requiem for Rome gave us a good an logical explanation for that: basically, the Sanctum was originally a jewish faction of the Peregrine Collegia, which was hicjacked by Longinists, and became the Lancea et Sanctum. So the Dammitic Creed would have been the original Creed.<br /> <br /> But I cannot see the Iblic Creed in any form. Specially, after centuries being an independent covenant (Bau Shaitan), suddenly they are absorved by the Sanctified. I can see them as an offring of Sanctified (may be founded by a Sanctified converted to Islam), so they could have also Theban Sorcery, but definitively, they should be an independent covenant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","user":"Uxas","date":". 04-19-2015, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T05:50:45-07:00","id":486270,"title":"","content":"&quot;Absorbed by.&quot; Putting aside that the Banu Shaitan reconciled with the Lancein the 19th Century and &quot;joined ranks,&quot; so that officially by the end of 1e, the Benu Shaitan and the Iblic Creed were both Lance creeds, its not like either Iblic or Banu Shaitan suddenly changing what they do or teach, merely whom they're enemies of. Its not like the Lance is some monolithic entity like the Roman Catholic Church that has oversight, and &quot;absorbs&quot; other religions under its umbrella. Every city is its own thing, where the local head priest decides everything; the Benu Shaitan may have reconcile, may have shared rituals, but they haven't suddenly started acting Catholic here. If you're divided into two Creeds fighting over who's the real vampire religion? Well, that's not anything new. Christians are well known for persecuting variations on their own faith, as well as Jewish and Islamic people, when they really should be trying to understand each other. <br /> <br /> Remember, the Benu Shaitan were introduced in a setting that involved the Crusades, a series of wars between two similar faiths in real life. Its well within theme for vampires to fight over who's got the &quot;right&quot; version of religion, both because religious zealotry, and because vampire, and because good excuse to fight about territory. This is really little different than European countries who invade each other, and catholic priests tell their soldiers that their enemies are wrong, and God wants them punished, or Islamic factions believing that their interpretation of the holy book is right, and anyone who disagrees, even other Muslims, should be put to death. <br /> <br /> Also note that the entire chapter that described the Benu Shaitan also included an Acolyte equivalent in the <i>Jinni</i>, Knightly Orders, Invictus and <i>Al-Amin</i>, and so on. The chapter describes two cultures that are mirrors of each other, set on opposing sides.<br /> <br /> So while the Benu Shaitan might have had a different history than Monochal L+S, they have similar beliefs in how vampires should act, they've been the academics and mystics of their region, and they have always have used Theban Sorcery. At that point? It doesn't matter. Benu Shaitan would use the library-enhanced LS specific merits in the Requiem core book; its thematic for them to use the new merits we're talking about here. We are discussing bringing in Islamic and Jewish influences into Theban Rituals. <br /> <br /> So, even if you want to call them separate covenants, its doesn't matter. Catholic-based Monochal creeds are not the only ones who use Theban, and we should see that reflected in the rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T08:47:17-07:00","id":486433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, even if you want to call them separate covenants, its doesn't matter. Catholic-based Monochal creeds are not the only ones who use Theban, and we should see that reflected in the rituals. </div> </div> </div>Sure but not under the Lancea et Sanctum. Rather like said they should have their own word-count devoted to them and their variations of Theban, or as the case might be Totally-not-Theban-Sorcery-Honest (thanks Elfive).<br /> <br /> There is only limited space in this book in particular devoted to Lancea et Sanctum and that word-count should be used to describe Lancea et Sanctum not the Islam/Judaism/someotherreligion if we are to do justice to any of them. Believe me the word-count of this book is likely only able to scratch the surface of what could be written about Catholic Vampires, or rather formerly Catholic, let alone have the space to adequately describe few other world religions from Vampiric point of view.<br /> <br /> Think of it like this. Either we get a small chapter for each religion that is shallow and somewhat unlikely to be of that much use or we get a full portion of this book about Lancea et Sanctum and later a full portion of some other book about Benu Shaitan etc. I don't know about you but I would vastly prefer the latter than the former.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T13:50:54-07:00","id":486709,"title":"","content":"In the original Covenant Book the Dammitc and Iblic creeds were presented as minor parts of the Lancea Sanctum but a different Faction there in as an attempt to make a blanket Covenant for the various Abrahamic Faiths. The problem with this is that each religion has mutually exclusive ideas, specifically pertaining to the Crucifixion and the details surrounding it. To be true to the mortal Faith each is based on they would have to either downplay the importance of the situation or change the details of it to fit their world view, both which would be at odds with the fundamental philosophy and Longinian Dogma that the Lancea et Sanctum is based upon.<br /> <br /> In the Dammatic Case Jesus would have had to be a Jewish teacher with no more importance than that. He wasn't the Messiah or a Prophet which reduces the role of Christ in the Crucifixion and the role that Longinus would have played in his own damnation. The entry even says that the creed dropped large portions of the Testament to make it a better fit for Jewish interpretation.<br /> <br /> For the Iblic Creed Jesus was a prophet, but not THE Prophet and the details of the Crucifixion's events would have had to change. He couldn't die on the Cross and was of lesser importance than Mohammed. He wasn't the sacrifice for the sins of man. Which, again, downplays the role of Longinus.<br /> <br /> The only one of the Three Abrahamic Faiths in which the Crucifixion was a World shattering event was Christianity, which is also the most Important event in the Lancea et Sanctum's religion.<br /> <br /> If you want to make different Covenants based off those religions, fine, if you want to lend them some credibility or mystical powers give them Theban Sorcery with uniquely flavored rituals or something else entirely. The issue is that they are odd fits for the Lancea et Sanctum. Particularly with the game's larger (Though not exclusive) focus on the Western Civilization and the books Focus on each Covenant.<br /> <br /> And as for the Exotheists, that was a blanket term for any Lancea et Sanctum Kindred that believed that the Vampiric religion shouldn't copy mortal faith and should be their own thing. Exotheists could believe that Christianity was the True Religion for mortals but that the Lancea et Sanctum shouldn't be modeled off of it.<br /> <br /> And an important idea to note is that the Brood and Livian Heresy would but just that, Heresies and enemies of the wider Covenant so their belief system wouldn't have a bearing on the Covenant philosophy as a whole.<br /> <br /> So I don't think a Catholic-flavored spell is an odd fit for a Covenant that is largely Christian and Catholic based.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3581,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3581-salubri87","user":"Salubri87","date":". 04-20-2015, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3581-salubri87","name":"Salubri87","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T15:27:58-07:00","id":486764,"title":"","content":"At the risk of getting yelled at, 2e seems to have already deviated from 1e in both design philosophy and fluff itself. I don't really think we should be using 1e fluff to dictate what is and isn't okay for 2e.<br /> <br /> I'd personally prefer the Sanctum be primarily Catholic while examining the impact this fact has on non-Catholic religious vampires, largely because the Sanctum is heavily influenced by Catholicism in at least 2e, than trying to fit them all under one umbrella for... why, exactly? These faiths were at each others' throats all throughout history. I doubt they'd put all that aside just because they turned into vampires.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm happy with whatever so long as 2e fluff remains consistent with 2e, disregarding 1e entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T06:03:39-07:00","id":489407,"title":"","content":"Very little jumped out at me as a problem in this document. By and large I really like what you've presented here, and I'm looking forward to using it in play. <br /> <br /> <b>Crusade</b> is fun, flavorful, and cool. The covenant fighting styles having effects that are borderline magic is just fine with me, you see similar effects from Temple Guardian and the Impaled. Some tightened guidelines on what sorts of powers are hampered by it would be good (what other supernatural powers count as &quot;sorcery&quot; in your conception?) Scaling its penalty to Merit dots rather than Weaponry is a good suggestion, and I add my support to that. <br /> <br /> <b>Flock </b>is great, as is <b>Temple of Damnation</b>. One of my favorite things in reading these playtest docs is going &quot;Oh man, that would have been perfect for this part of that game I ran...&quot; Temple of Damnation in particular in inspirational in that regard and is already spawning ideas. <br /> <br /> <b>Laity</b>. The effects are solid, but I'm not sold on the name. I was under the impression that &quot;laity&quot; referred to members of the L+S that aren't anointed priests. Not a huge quibble, but I'm a fan of clarity in terms and this seems a bit muddy. <br /> <br /> <b>Sanctuary</b>. Solomon Birch and his &quot;Solomon Swastikas,&quot; anyone? Sold. <br /> <br /> <b>Stigmata</b>. Love it. As for the question of what benefit it provides to a mortal, I didn't see anyone note this in the discussion so apologies if I missed it, but a mortal with Stigmata heals lethal damage at double the normal rate. That's a pretty handy benefit, and makes that mortal a serious asset to the covenant, and specifically to any vampire who feeds on them normally. <br /> <br /> <b>Apple of Eden</b>. It can grant attributes above 5, can the affected character spend Experiences to KEEP an attribute above 5? <br /> <br /> <b>Marian Apparition</b>. The menstrual blood in the sacrament might be a reference to the &quot;black Madonnas&quot; of Italy, which are highly venerated for being miraculous, and there are some lines of thought linking those miraculous icons to power inherent in menstruation.<br /> <br /> <b>Revelatory Shroud</b>. Very cool, but it's a one-dot ritual treading on what it otherwise takes Auspex 3 to accomplish. Granted it's slightly more narrow in focus, but only slightly. <br /> <br /> The rest of the rituals are solid. I particularly love <b>Pledge to the Worthless One</b>. <b>Great Prophecy</b> is extremely cool, and the outline seems to keep it tight in scope while leaving it a versatile tool for whatever a given game requires, not to mention the sacrament required. That should keep it from being flung around willy-nilly, which could become a problem. Really well done.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T20:10:36-07:00","id":495669,"title":"","content":"Got some great stuff here. I, too, read many things there and thought &quot;that would have worked perfectly for X character/situation&quot;.<br /> <br /> A few questions and points. I absolutely support changing <b>Marian Apparition</b> so its name and description do not explicitly define who or what the apparition is. It's much more interesting to me if each viewer may interpret the apparition differently as something perhaps very personal to them.<br /> <br /> What happens if the holly switch prepared for <b>Apparition of the Host</b> is snapped accidentally? Or by somebody who doesn't know is effects?<br /> <br /> The horn using in <b>The Walls of Jericho</b> remains empowered for seven nights. May I use it more than once within that period? It crumbles at the ritual's end. It is not entirely clear when that end is.<br /> <br /> <b>The Guiding Star</b> allows coin-holders to find a supernaturally safe place. The text says <span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">the Storyteller comes up with a location&quot;. Does this location have to already exist? Not every domain will have a sanctum so marvelous. Is an already existent safe place improved? Does a safe place spring up behind an abandoned door, sort of thing?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Overall I'm loving the direction taken with the disciplines and sorceries of 2nd Ed. Less subtlety, in some places. More out and out supernatural occurences. More open-ended powers like the illusions of nightmare and obfuscate. Wonderful varied applications.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1230-thenagain","name":"thenagain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T09:39:53-07:00","id":496381,"title":"","content":"How do you make those rituals??<br /> I take Blood and Sacrament as a guide but then i get thing like Pledge to the Worthless One and i dont know what to make of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T09:47:17-07:00","id":496386,"title":"","content":"Several of the rituals described in the open dev documents sort of defy the Theme system from Sacraments and Blasphemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T12:35:42-07:00","id":496602,"title":"","content":"I doubt the writers are going to be using the Blasphemes and Sacraments book as gospel going forwards. Its provided an alternative system, yes. Emphasis on the word alternative. Its not exactly a core book system. Why slave yourself to a system when it gets in the way of ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T01:01:02-07:00","id":497213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/478606-lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles?p=496602#post496602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt the writers are going to be using the Blasphemes and Sacraments book as gospel going forwards. Its provided an alternative system, yes. Emphasis on the word alternative. Its not exactly a core book system. Why slave yourself to a system when it gets in the way of ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because those same ideas could have been used for all of these rituals? Perhaps with an addition of saying that the theme X is also capable of Y. Or clearly giving a bigger drawback and saying that this works, because it gives you more power for bigger price, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T20:02:15-07:00","id":511483,"title":"","content":"Thats why im asking how do they make them. Because i have no idea how and only have BS as a guide.<br /> The cruac ritual Bounty of the storm in something that i couldnt even think of and couldnt even see as a possible effect for cruac if i didnt see it first.<br /> I dont really understand how Curse of aphrodite is a level 3 ritual when it causes the effect of 4 dot discipline<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1351,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","user":"Sakii","date":". 05-11-2015, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T22:39:17-07:00","id":511686,"title":"","content":"Transmutation 2 dots -alters speech<br /> Transmutation 4 dots -control physical actions<br /> <br /> Curse of Aphrodite 3 dots - Charmed, Enthralled, Obsession, Swooned<br /> <br /> I think it fits pretty well between 2 and 4 Transmutation.<br /> <br /> I have no idea about Bounty of the Storm. I guess that the long wait time for the storm is waiting for proper conditions which would put it at Creation 3. The wealth thing is beyond my understanding, but bumping it up a dot makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T08:40:07-07:00","id":512014,"title":"","content":"um, so maybe it does fit. I just always saw blood sorcery as less powerful but more versatile that disciplines so seeing one doing something more powerful went against my preconceptions.<br /> <br /> My thing with Bounty of the Storm is more one of theme, cruac is bloody and viceral so a storm that gives you wealth is something that wouldnt fit there the way i see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:33:52-07:00","id":512054,"title":"","content":"The thematic idea behind Bounty of the Storm is the acolyte belief that suffering brings growth. Whereas Theban Sorcery could transmute dross into gold, the Circle doesn't believe in such neat, easy, clean solutions to anything. So for them to gain wealth through sorcery there must be trial, and suffering. The ritual causes, potentially, quite a bit of death. 2/3 of the bystanders around the target of the ritual when the storm strikes end up dead. The caster risks humanity loss, the target is physically punished. In return for all that, some form of wealth comes to the target. Could be settlements, insurance claims, any of several different sources for the actual money (or the equivalent).<br /> <br /> Suffering for gain is very Circle. You need a lot of money in a relative hurry? Okay. But it'll cost you, and everyone around you.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And lest we forget, the ritual destroys an object of personal significance to the victim. How many &quot;deeply personal objects&quot; that aren't touchstones do vampires keep around? Some, sure. Probably not terribly many in most cases. Nothing given, nothing gained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","user":"Smarmy Vamp","date":". 05-12-2015, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}